{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1365834-lostlight-reads-hunter-2e","id":1365834,"title":"LostLight Reads Hunter 2E","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-02-06T14:03:03-08:00","id":1365834,"title":"LostLight Reads Hunter 2E","content":"So, Hunter is by far my most favorite CofD game, and I can't say how excited I am for finally getting the Kickstarter. As such, I am going to detail my experience of reading the manuscript in this thread in real time. God, this is so awesome, I can't wait!<br /> <br /> Anyway, here we go-<br /> <br /> opening quote- awesome.<br /> <br /> God, it looks exactly like I imagined it to be.<br /> <br /> I really like how the book describes the Vigil- hope and despair is such a strong theme, and the imagery is beautiful.<br /> <br /> Si it seems that compacts and conspiracies still use Status to grant benefits. I knew that the whole attempt to translate those groups to Mystery Cults was too early!<br /> <br /> wooooooowwww I like the concept of Mythics... In think I found a new way to integrate the Navio de Tolos to 2e.<br /> <br /> There seems to be Bygones as something more accessible to all hunters? Perhaps that's why the AKD were removed from being a core group in 2e...<br /> <br /> Not sure that I get the concept of rogue cells from the description- I know the 1e definition of cancer cells, but what does it mean &quot;operate on their own&quot; as being differ from any 1st tier cell?<br /> <br /> Wait- if rippers are still humans, does it mean the Code still states to protect them?<br /> <br /> I really love the whole &quot;low on information&quot; feeling that Hunter have. Something bumps at the night, but you have no idea WHAT it is.<br /> <br /> I really like the fact the Hunter's terminology is more or less the one I use for writing. No need for drastic changes in wrietups from that POV.<br /> <br /> Oh, the Mortal Instruments is on the inspiration list! Natural, of course, but I usually don't recognize the inspirations :P<br /> <br /> Chapter One's opening quote- cool<br /> <br /> So it seems that Touchstones and losing them will be tied to become a Slasher. At least, that was what I hoped it to be.<br /> <br /> So professions as a concept are still around, I'm just not sure if they have any mechanical support. Nice touch that the book makes a clear distinction between tiers of game.<br /> <br /> The concept of &quot;joining a compact/conspiracy is a compromise&quot; seems to run deep in this book. nice.<br /> <br /> So research and investigation is going to be a main theme of playing Hunter- as it should be.<br /> <br /> I really like it that the Vigil almost feels like a sentient thing. the whole &quot;the Vigil as a virus&quot; comes really strong from the writeup. Really cool.<br /> <br /> ohhhhh I really like Hunter politics.<br /> <br /> I really do enjoy the description of the Hunter society<br /> <br /> Ah, my favorite- Conspiracies<br /> <br /> So it seems like the history of Cheiron is playing a big role in the book. Nice, I like to see the setting evolves.<br /> <br /> So it seems that Endowments are going to be less stable and more flexible in 2e. Interesting.<br /> <br /> And History Section!<br /> <br /> Not sure if I'm reading it right- but are the Keepers of the Weave and the Scarlet Watch still around? Because if so- awesome! Compacts also seems to be far more localized in space and time, which may explain the Followers of Mansa from DE2. <br /> <br /> So the Barrett Commission is no longer around? Oh well...<br /> <br /> The One seems like a very interesting plot hook. A bit direct, but still interesting.<br /> <br /> THE NIBIRU<br /> <br /> AVES MINERVA<br /> <br /> The Ordo de Quirinus sound like a very pre modern version of VALKYRIE<br /> <br /> The Scenes of the Forbidden are nice.<br /> <br /> The Ahl al Jabal cameo. Cool.<br /> <br /> So the Bear Lodge has also collapsed, being absorbed in the Ashwood Abbey while originally being formed from the Les Voyageurs (?). I'm not sure how I feel about the canon fall of two splats, but them being absorbed into the Abbey does make sense. Make it three.<br /> <br /> Again, I'm a bit torn about the loss of some of those compacts. While it does emphasis strongly the unstable nature of compacts and the evolution of the Vigil, I believe some of those groups have their fans, and I'm not sure how they feel about it. None of those evolution seems unnatural, however- they make a lot of sense, add dynamism for the setting and emphasis the temporary nature of compacts and the dangers of the Vigil- but still.<br /> <br /> Wait- the Merrick Institution is gone?! That's... disappointing, saying the least. Or are they talking about the Institution that created the traumatic children? Because that would make much more sense.<br /> <br /> Yeah, those hunters who think they can tell the Promethean Brotherhood and the Abbey what to do can go and *************[REDACTED]**. On the other hand- I do have plans for them... (evil laughter)<br /> <br /> Ohh Los Angelitos! A new compact on which only the name is known! Cool!<br /> <br /> So the Council of Bones really seem to fill the scholar type conspiracy niche.<br /> <br /> Hey- you CAN'T make up an awesome name for a conspiracy such as the Five Roses Empire and just say that it was DISBANDED! Come On!<br /> <br /> I WANT THE BAN GAISGEDAIG<br /> <br /> A node for Fallen Blossoms. Nice.<br /> <br /> The Archive of the Lucifuge is everything I ever wanted it to be.<br /> <br /> And here comes Chapter 2...<br /> <br /> So the Watch and the Keepers are apparently not around, I think.. at least, not as they were.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure SWORN are for my liking, but I guess we'll see how it goes?<br /> <br /> So the Ashwood are in the book, as well as the AKD! Awesome! The Nine Stars also seem to be very interesting.<br /> <br /> Endowments- yeahhhhhh<br /> <br /> Endowments as a gamble is a very nice twist.<br /> <br /> Perispiritism sounds like a very nice name for Endowments.<br /> <br /> It seems that Endowments will be different from the Playtest version (I don't remember if it was rated in that version). Again, there is a reason you shouldn't revise homebrew to 2E before it comes out.<br /> <br /> Aaand that's it, for now at least. More on February 8th!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-06T14:15:58-08:00","id":1365838,"title":"","content":"Waaaaaaaaaaaait. Hunter is your favorite game? Well shock and motherfucking awe. Who'd ever guess that one? \ud83e\udd2f\ud83d\ude02","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-06T16:10:59-08:00","id":1365876,"title":"","content":"I'll admit, I already said it once, I'm not happy at all with the compacts falling. Division 6 for one I know has many fans for being a subversion of &quot;secret government organization, and personally I just dont like the purposeful taking down of any previously established organizations (one of the reasons I'm sad about the Abbey and AKD not being full splats)<br /> <br /> I know these seem natural, but the bear lodge values nothing of the abbey (even if their stereotype hinted at it), the Commission makes sense in a way, but their whole ethos was being virtually unknown and keeping to politics/business/military affairs. they just dont fit being part of Men in Black.<br /> <br /> who knows, maybe there will be a compacts and conspiracies vol 2 that brings back the original supplement organizations. again, it's likely just me being selfish, but I dont think new, stated to be active, organizations should be marginalized.<br /> <br /> big fan of the terminology and the pseudomystical take on the Vigil itself, and 9 stars, well I loved sleeping dogs, so I should love them","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-08T05:25:08-08:00","id":1366298,"title":"","content":"And here comes the second preview!<br /> <br /> First, here are some songs you should listen to when reading Hunter-<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=bYznBldN7OY\" target=\"_blank\">We are the Others- Delain</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=2m57ia5wuwA\" target=\"_blank\">Paradise- Within Temptation ft Tarja</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Mpea-VSJYnE&amp;list=RDMpea-VSJYnE&amp;start_radio=1\" target=\"_blank\">Welcome to the Black Parade- My Chemical Romance Cover by Postmodern Jukebox</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=LdRvv2U4y-E\" target=\"_blank\">Innocent Sorrow- Abingdon Boys School</a><br /> <br /> And of course, in honor for the Slasher Chronicles:<br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=o0u4M6vppCI\" target=\"_blank\">Shia LaBeouf- Rob Cantor</a><br /> <br /> with that out of the way- let's start on reading, shall we?<br /> <br /> Ohhh cool art for the Ascending Ones. I like it.<br /> <br /> Yeah, the Long Night are full power Apocalypse Cult.<br /> <br /> Well, it seem they have also went full power on the theme of &quot;desperate hope&quot; of the book. The End of Time is here, and you are not good enough for Heaven.<br /> <br /> Yeah, I can definitely see the touch of Compacts &amp; Conspiracies in the writeup.<br /> <br /> I must say that I do like how the writeup moves from hope to despair. One moment, the end of times is coming and Satan is about to devour the world. On the other, by believing that it is the Apocalypse, you also believe that the Second Coming will soon happen. The dichotomy between an hopeless battle and clinging to hope and faith is a great opening for the first writeup in the book, IMO.<br /> <br /> Yeah, the Long Night just throwing all monsters into the &quot;demon&quot; category makes tons of sense for them.<br /> <br /> So who said they can't play monster redeemers in 2e? Because if you were afraid it would be the case, apparently, it is not.<br /> <br /> In general, it looks like they have kept the 1e structure for Hunter writeup. As most 2e games changed it, I am a bit surprised. Not that it is a bad thing, just somewhat surprising.<br /> <br /> Yeah, the Doctrines are still here, almost unchanged I believe.<br /> <br /> Ah, finally, Status benefits- yes, the same concept as 1e.<br /> <br /> Again, I need to say it- awesome art for the Ascending Ones.<br /> <br /> Woooooooooow, I really like that quote. I wonder if they are going to embrace the Mummy angle from Mortal Remains.<br /> <br /> So some interesting description for the development of Elixirs. It is far less mythic than how their original writeup was, which helps to actually ground them in history, which is cool.<br /> <br /> Yeah, they are still global drug dealers and underground doctors.<br /> <br /> Ammm tasty plot hook is indeed tasty. I wonder if the leaders of the Ascending Ones plan to prepare to some coming danger (*cough*ARISEN*cough*) or if they are the ones who were touched by the corruption.<br /> <br /> Again, we can clearly see that the &quot;all monsters must be slain&quot; kind of hunter is far from the default concept. Yeah, the concept of Sulha between monsters is still a thing, and them being known as &quot;neutral emissaries&quot; between monster organizations both makes sense and is extremely ironic on the same time.<br /> <br /> Interesting- so the Ascending Ones are a fractured organization, only slightly better than groups such as Les Mysteres and the Cainte Heresy. Interesting.<br /> <br /> I really like how the Hunter description shows the three faces of the AO- faith, crime and mysticism, all touched by alchemy.<br /> <br /> Kinda surprised there was no mention of Akhenaten by name in the writeup. Also, no Mummy reference. Oh well.<br /> <br /> Yeah, the idea that each of the three factions is almost independent from one another is still a thing.<br /> <br /> It looks like the Knife of Paradise is less connected to extremist religious groups than it was in 1e, as far as I remember. The Jagged Crescent are still the criminal organization we all know and love, and the Order is as hermetic as ever.<br /> <br /> So thankfully, the first point of Status among conspiracies isn't now just &quot;you can buy dots in the X Endowments&quot;<br /> <br /> yeah yeah, same old Endowments section from the earlier preview<br /> <br /> Basically, the alchemy of the Ascending Ones is transforming poison into salvation, with faith serving as the furnace. Nice.<br /> <br /> With the emphasis on internal alchemy, I'm surprised there was no mention of Tao or a Chinese branch in the writeup.<br /> <br /> Again, a strong hint that something is wrong about the AO's hunters- but what?<br /> <br /> Oh, so it includes the mechanics for making new Elixirs. Cool. Now you are not just a user, but also a researcher (support for an Order member)<br /> <br /> I like the presentation of the Elixirs. It shows that the true Endowment is not the potion itself, but the ability to transform the poison into power. You are Endowed with recipes, knowledge and discipline to transform the reagents into an Elixir, not just a ready made potion. I wonder if that counts for them being Sleepwalkers and/or Kin for Beasts.<br /> <br /> Looking at the Endowments, Amun's Water seems the most out of place- most of them have some alchemical transformation of the body and or mind. this one turns you outright invisible. Weird- not bad, but weird.<br /> <br /> Again, I knew people shouldn't start converting Endowments to the Condition structure before it was official.<br /> <br /> So someone tries to take over the resources which hunters use to work. I wonder if this plot hook is meant to discourage cross-conspiracy games, or serve as a plot hook for one.<br /> <br /> I must say that something feels reaaaaaaally weird in the previews until now. It is full of dynamism to the point the changes happen right now in the hunter society, as if there is a preparation for something which is going to change. Usually, Core books are meant to be more or less static- you get the writeups, splats and mechanics, and assume there won't be any radical changes unless there will be a new edition. Even then, most 2e's changes were rectons instead of progression in time. Perhaps the &quot;static' state for Hunter 2e is that change is coming and nothing is stable. Strange- again, not bad, just very strange. I wonder if it is going to continue in the rest of the writeups.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":503,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","user":"LostLight","date":". 02-08-2020, 09:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-10T14:21:19-08:00","id":1366859,"title":"","content":"So let's see what Hunter has given me for my birthday, shall we?<br /> <br /> Interesting that considering the strong ties the history section had with Dark Eras that there is no tie in between the Loyalists of Thule's writeup in their origin in Into the Cold.<br /> <br /> Again, I see that the Loyalists' writeup is very Compacts and Conspiracies inspired. the Three Old Men which hate each other to death while united by common debt makes a great hook for the group.<br /> <br /> Again, an organization on the edge and the fear of being compromised. Dynamism and instability is a very strong theme of this book, and I assume means to encourage you, as a ST, to make your own groups or replace others as you wish.<br /> <br /> Also, my pet theory- the Three Old Men were so invested in their hatred and debt and work, that they never noticed that they have died, and still work to maintain the compact. My idea is that eventually, after rediscovering the ghosts of the romoahals, they would absorb the ancient ghosts and create some sort of eldritch network of information, leading the compact into becoming a conspiracy. Again, just how I would play thing out.<br /> <br /> Also, weird that there is no mention of the romoahals.<br /> <br /> Yeah, so I personally feel that the writeup leads towards the Loyalists being on the way of becoming a conspiracy (or dying out. It is always an option)<br /> <br /> I wonder if the book is going to suggest WHY there is a rise in the supernatural's activity. No other 2e game suggest that something is brewing under the surface, but it is clear that something is going on from Hunter's perspective.<br /> <br /> Yep, the Loyalists are definitely NOT nice.<br /> <br /> I think that the whole &quot;tomb raider&quot; angle that the AKD had is more covered now by some of the Loyalists. Still, we are getting the AKD, so we'll see the differences later on.<br /> <br /> Yep, risking Willpower is still a thing.<br /> <br /> I must say that Cheiron's art is less evocative than the AO's, IMO.<br /> <br /> Why the hell the &quot;House of Katz&quot; sound some familiar?..<br /> <br /> So Katz is an abbreviation of &quot;priest of justice&quot; in hebrew, Helios is often connected to Apollo which is the god of healing among many others, and I can't find something about Octavian and healing, but I guess it may have been Cheiron's Roman incarnation.<br /> <br /> I think I remember the logo on a sword or shield of Roman centurion from Witch Finders- but no mention of Santorini? A missed opportunity, IMO.<br /> <br /> Like, seriously- are you trying to claim that the average citizen in the world thinks that a pharmaceuticals company are NOT the devil? I mean, no matter how much money they spill for philanthropy and medical treatment, no one I knows thinks that those companies actually care about anyone but making money from sick people- and that's before taking into account that this is the CofD's version of our world.<br /> <br /> Melanie Sweetwater- yeah, sure. That's definitely NOT a suspicious name...<br /> <br /> I wonder that if Cheiron is Wolfram and Hart, then Sweetwater is Eve?<br /> <br /> Like, I'm starting to wonder how many of the abbreviations fans use were canon before 2e. I mean, we have already seen TFV and now TCG- and I honesty can't recall if I have ever seen those being used in the books. Oh well.<br /> <br /> Pension? Ah! I want to see one FPD agent reaching old age and actually enjoying that benefit.<br /> <br /> Yeah, Cheiron are as evil as always (which is, as evil as any company is, with some unknown agendas)<br /> <br /> Again- instability in CHEIRON. Now, that's a terrifying thought. I would play with the rouge agents turning to my homebrew Ningishzida crime syndicate. This plot hook works well with my Civil Wars suggestion for them.<br /> <br /> So the DPT are practically NPCs in universe.<br /> <br /> Ok- what is the &quot;incident&quot;? Is the the Beast that went rampage and brought down Cheiron's offices in Tokyo, from that fiction?<br /> <br /> And seriously- an even MORE useless version of the field resources manual? Can they PLEASE make it a stretch goal to make it an actual book, like the Testament of Longinus and Dreams of Avarice? Why do other gamelines get all of the fun?<br /> <br /> &quot;Now you have new nightmares&quot; is, like, the best sentence in this book until now :P<br /> <br /> Yeah, your first test to encrypting the code for your manual- where your life depends on it.<br /> <br /> &quot;Sweetwater is watching&quot; is almost as good as the previous quote.<br /> <br /> Thaumatech being a bleeding edge science my *****. Organ transplant doesn't work like this, and they know it. This is some voodoo madness and fleshcraft that could make the Tzimisce feel impressed.<br /> <br /> Yeah, there is no way out from Cheiron with all of your pieces inside.<br /> <br /> Yeah, I guess that with too many implants, the agent is going to go Deviant instead.<br /> <br /> I do like the transplant mechanics.<br /> <br /> Again, I must wonder if when the hunter reach a maximal amount of Endowments, are they considered sleepwalkers/kin. The second option is probably horrifying for the Beasts who witness it.<br /> <br /> I wonder if the new version of the manual was in fact written by the rouge cell of P.R, and if they are somehow connected to the &quot;incident&quot;- or maybe it was the last thing the conspiracy managed to capture before their escape.<br /> <br /> It is more likely that Cheiron stole the hand from the AKD than from the AO.<br /> <br /> The swarm is seriously terrifying. I feel like I should get that reference, but I don't know what it should mean.<br /> <br /> Now I want to know from where the sonic resonance attenuator comes from.<br /> <br /> Goddamn it, they put pieces of mummies inside of people?!<br /> <br /> Anyway, a very cool writeup for Cheiron and the Loyalists. Some missed opportunists for the lack of references such as Santorini, Into the Cold and the romoahals, but overall very nice. Kudos on the flesh horrors. I can definitely say it is the best birthday present I got today (sure, it is the only one- unless the stray cat counts, but still).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-11T02:00:26-08:00","id":1366930,"title":"","content":"Thank you for the post and Happy Birthday LostLight.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-12T07:20:04-08:00","id":1367213,"title":"","content":"And here comes the time for Network 0 and the brand new Council of Bones!<br /> <br /> Full disclosure- as the AKD were, like my second favorite conspiracy (right after the Lucifuge, and in some days even more than them), I am going to be very critical with those who took their place as a core group. Not that I won't be fair, but I'm going to give them a very good look. I believe they are going to be good, don't take me wrong- but if there will be something about them I won't like I won't sugarcoat it.<br /> <br /> But first thing -first- Network 0!<br /> <br /> Lol- I do like the fact that even in the CofD, Slenderman is fake... or, at least, it was. I mean, what that real is not important- what you think is real does.<br /> <br /> So here is one group which thinks that humanity SHOULD know that there are monsters in the dark. That puts them in conflict with not only the monsters, but also with most hunters.<br /> <br /> Also- does that mean that the drone person's art was NOT a Network 0 art? I was sure it was.. maybe it is Valkyrie or VASCU, then?<br /> <br /> Yeah, I guess that some of those trolls were actual trolls. We have enough monsters who know how to use the internet and would not like to get exposed by hunters. Others could be hunters of other conspiracies who launched a cyber attack on NW-0's credibility- VALKYRIE, I'm looking at you!<br /> <br /> I guess that such a setback for Network 0 was expected- the pitch for the group was when the internet was still seen as a way to connect the world to all information and allowing everyone to know everything. Now, you CAN'T believe the internet, and even videos are not enough ton convince people due to Deep Fake and all of that. Network 0 must change attitude or develop their tools even further- both which could lead into them growing into a conspiracy, if they'll survive.<br /> <br /> Live feed hunts? Yeah, that can't end badly :P<br /> <br /> In wonder is a possible merge between Network 0 and the Null Mysteriis is what the future holds- it would help them ground their claims in reality and give them contacts and academic support. Add to that a merge with the Loyalists of Thule (even though their agendas clash hardly), and an information based conspiracy may rise from the mix.<br /> <br /> Oh- I must say I feel sad for that vampire. They were probably mid humanity level one, as they tried not to kill the hunter. They may have even seen them as a Touchstone for them. Oh well, they are dead now.<br /> <br /> Yeah, I think that the Army of Truth is destined to fall down, and the Secret Keepers merging with with the Loyalists)<br /> <br /> And now- the Council of Bones.<br /> <br /> Yeah, hunters who don't fear death means a LOT of problem for monsters :P<br /> <br /> I do like the occultist network kind of things which is going on for them- but how can they hate the undead and still work with ghosts?<br /> <br /> So the Council dies and is being reborn constantly? Makes you wonder what exactly keeps it alive..<br /> <br /> Thinking on that, wouldn't the rise and fall of the group is somewhat similar to the rise and fall of Krewes?<br /> <br /> Yeah, the title of the &quot;first hunters&quot; belongs to the Nibiru.<br /> <br /> I really do like their origin myth, however- I would have liked it to be a bit more expanded, actually.<br /> <br /> Overall looks nice- some things rings a bell a bit with my homebrew Ebony Fangs. Some rework may be needed for their transition for 2e, but I think that their niche as exiles and outcasts is strong enough to allow them to stand on their own.<br /> <br /> I assume that the Council clashes quite a bit with Slashers, making them a good material for 2e. In general, I feel like the new organizations tends towards a more universal attitude towards monsters, and are less focused around a specific kind of monsters.<br /> <br /> I must say I'm curious about why there isn't much about the history of the Council's earlier incarnations compared to the Ascending Ones and Cheiron. It is very specific about the current organization, which looks like it is very fractured in structure, and doesn't say much about other forms it was rebuilt. I would have expected a shout out for 1001 Nightmares, as they were mentioned there.<br /> <br /> So mediums that don't work as mediums is a bit strange- why it enhance that most other mediums are either fake or being manipulated by monsters, I would have expected it as a natural way the group would work. A somewhat chivalrous choice, I think. Maybe that medium from Paranormal Activity was a member of the group.<br /> <br /> Maybe the Council is the one responsible for denying organizations their very needed resources?<br /> <br /> I must say that the Council is a bit too &quot;clean&quot; for me- sure, there is a certain amount of hypocrisy in the way they view themselves as one of the few &quot;clean&quot; conspiracies (as their Endowments are &quot;natural&quot;), but I feel they are styled as without the dark side I like for my organizations.<br /> <br /> I do like the hunter sections, however.<br /> <br /> Using the dead while being constantly on the watch of being manipulated may be the reason why the Les Mysteres were dissolved, from meta perspective.<br /> <br /> Again, Perispiritism is a great name for an Endowment.<br /> <br /> I would really like to see the Council in the Age of Spiritualism Dark Era.<br /> <br /> I personally think that the Mark is actually a parasitic entity made from the remains of a ghost, bound the their host like a geist.<br /> <br /> I would say that hunters murdering those who use their Endowments before others is a bit extreme- but considering they don;t see death as much of an issue I can understand where they are coming from.<br /> <br /> I do wonder what the numbers in the eyes of the skull means.. maybe no hunter of the Council can live beyond 99? The life of an hunter are dangerous, after all.<br /> <br /> I do like how the Council leave messages upon the Twilight.<br /> <br /> I don't think that I have seen any limit or way to learn new Endowments for the Council, which is different from the ones granted to the AO and Cheiron.<br /> <br /> So the Council can actually turn ghosts into hand puppet? Yea, that's disgusting<br /> <br /> I must admit that with all of their fear from the Twilight, what do you think will happen if a Council member will visit the UNDERWORLD?<br /> <br /> Aaand the preview died for some reason? I'll complete whatever left and my finale thoughts for when ti would return<br /> <br /> EDIT- and it is back again!<br /> <br /> And I actually have nothing more to end!<br /> <br /> Overall, I really liked Network 0's writeup. Something about the Council a bit bothers me, and I'm not sure what. Some lack of consistency, maybe? Or maybe they were not what I expected them to be? I mean, they are not bad or anything, but I'm just not strongly into them... Again, I may be biased, as I mentally compare them to my own homebrew conspiracies and for them taking the place of the AKD as a core group. Still, something just robs me the wrong way about them, and I can't say what.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":503,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","user":"LostLight","date":". 02-12-2020, 10:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-12T17:25:56-08:00","id":1367340,"title":"","content":"I think you hit the nail on the head when you said too clean. They seem to only hunt the bad monsters like vampires and zombies. well staying cool with the good monsters like witches or sin eaters. I would have liked a more adversary type relationship with at least sin eaters. maybe seeing them as ghosts controlling humans and how that is bad. something like that.<br /> <br /> That and they match too closely with Krewes for my taste.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24179-grimmi05","name":"Grimmi05","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-12T17:55:22-08:00","id":1367345,"title":"","content":"Their biases based on undeath rather than personage and their susceptibilty to being a tool of ghosts is plenty problematic. There's also clearly something missing in their understanding of their relationship to the legacy and mecahnics of the Conspiracy that <i>does not bode well</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 02-12-2020, 08:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-12T19:00:14-08:00","id":1367357,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1365834-lostlight-reads-hunter-2e?p=1367345#post1367345\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Their biases based on undeath rather than personage and their susceptibilty to being a tool of ghosts is plenty problematic. There's also clearly something missing in their understanding of their relationship to the legacy and mecahnics of the Conspiracy that <i>does not bode well</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>now that you mention it. they do seem to just want to raze whatever refuses to die (without even questioning whether they even WANTED to be undead to begin with)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar503_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"503\" data-vbnamecard=\"503\">LostLight</a>, I think the reason they are more kind to ghost is because it's a spiritual being, not bound in flesh. that, and most are trying to move on, but unable to until they either get destroyed or complete unfinished business","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-12T19:09:22-08:00","id":1367358,"title":"","content":"Yeah, the whole &quot;undead bad, unquiet good&quot; thing is something begging for a Reaper to pretend to be a &quot;concerned citizen&quot; and hunt those nasty ghostwalkers.<br /> <br /> Besides, they do have a pretty dark side; their inability to trust other conspiracies and antagonize other hunters they feel are doing it wrong. That's self-destructive.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-12T19:32:05-08:00","id":1367370,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1365834-lostlight-reads-hunter-2e?p=1367358#post1367358\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, the whole &amp;quot;undead bad, unquiet good&amp;quot; thing is something begging for a Reaper to pretend to be a &amp;quot;concerned citizen&amp;quot; and hunt those nasty ghostwalkers.<br /> <br /> Besides, they do have a pretty dark side; their inability to trust other conspiracies and antagonize other hunters they feel are doing it wrong. That's self-destructive.</div> </div> </div> </div>I did like that hypocrisy there. &quot;did that man just say he communed with God to do that? he can NOT be trusted. now let's go hunt that beast our ghost said killed him&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-12T20:06:31-08:00","id":1367381,"title":"","content":"Again, &quot;Probably Manipulated by Ghost Conspiracies&quot; is absolutely on that list of &quot;And You Think Being Funded by Vampires is Bad Somehow&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-12T21:44:05-08:00","id":1367390,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1365834-lostlight-reads-hunter-2e?p=1367381#post1367381\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again, &amp;quot;Probably Manipulated by Ghost Conspiracies&amp;quot; is absolutely on that list of &amp;quot;And You Think Being Funded by Vampires is Bad Somehow&amp;quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>to be honest, I never understood how being funded by monsters was such a huge deal breaker to so many people. like sure, they can influence TFV with taking some funding away, but they are largely unaware of just about everything else","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-12T21:57:40-08:00","id":1367394,"title":"","content":"Oh, the Council of Bones are, without doubt, hypocrites, and any group which kills any member of theirs simply by using their Endowment before others, if I read it correctly, definitely has a bad side, and they know that the ghosts can manipulate them. But something about them still feels off, for me- I can't put my finger on it. Maybe I expected too much to fall in love with them from first sight - I love ghost hunting groups, and I love scholar groups and I love oracular groups- but something doesn't click for me. I mean, the Cappodacians were one of my favorite Clans/Bloodlines in Masquerade, and each of the splats covers the same niche of &quot;scholars of death&quot; for their game, and still I can't put my finger on what doesn't clicks for me. I would have said it was their fractured structure and the lack of history in their writeup, but I still liked the Les Mysteres, so...<br /> <br /> Maybe it is a combination of factors, perhaps it is something I misread about them, maybe it is some unconscious bias for some of my own writings and the AKD, maybe it is something that I need to ponder about, maybe I just need to some time- not every love is from first sight, after all. Still, currently, something about them feels too clean for me- I think that the &quot;cleanliness&quot; that I feel is how focused they are on the Vigil. I am not sure how they fund themselves or integrate themselves into mortal society. They are too isolated, both in the Vigil and in the world. Something feels off with them lacking an actual connection- unlike the ghosts they &quot;care&quot; for, they feel like they drift through time and space, without something to anchor them, without some connection to the world. For being their most current incarnation, it feels like they are fading out...<br /> <br /> Again, it is not a bad writeup- they just don't &quot;click' for me, and I am not sure why. I think that it is their total devotion for their Vigil and isolation from the world, but again, it may not be the whole picture. Once I'll actually get it I'll post it, but for now I think that that's what disturbs me the most about them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-13T04:41:03-08:00","id":1367489,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1365834-lostlight-reads-hunter-2e?p=1367394#post1367394\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe it is a combination of factors, perhaps it is something I misread about them, maybe it is some unconscious bias for some of my own writings and the AKD, maybe it is something that I need to ponder about, maybe I just need to some time- not every love is from first sight, after all. Still, currently, something about them feels too clean for me-</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel exactly the same, too removed and with too little dirt on their hands. The good news there is that this is mostly an issue of fiction, and probably one that will be fixed simply as a result of the book being written as the various factions are given more character and we learn of how they interact with each other and the world at large. There's also a lack of something that I can best describe as 'immediacy', they don't seem to have any pressing issues to motivate them on a Conspiracy-wide scale (where L\u00e9s Mysteres have gauntlet breaches and the Forsaken all over the world, and we all always knew where the Cappadocians were headed), nothing seems to really unite them. Again I think this issue, while important, is relatively easily solved by pondering what their actual purpose is (beyond hunting ghosts) and who (or what) they keep pissing off to the point where it cuts their numbers in half. Cthonic gods?<br /> <br /> I may be wrong, but I think that most of this results from this being what-I-assume-to-be an early write-up, and later iterations could well fill in the blanks.<br /> In that spirit, as well as for fun, what would you alter, add or subtract from the current write-up of the Council of Bones?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24688-mrmeow","name":"MrMeow","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-13T05:18:01-08:00","id":1367497,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrMeow</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1365834-lostlight-reads-hunter-2e?p=1367489#post1367489\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I feel exactly the same, too removed and with too little dirt on their hands. The good news there is that this is mostly an issue of fiction, and probably one that will be fixed simply as a result of the book being written as the various factions are given more character and we learn of how they interact with each other and the world at large. There's also a lack of something that I can best describe as 'immediacy', they don't seem to have any pressing issues to motivate them on a Conspiracy-wide scale (where L\u00e9s Mysteres have gauntlet breaches and the Forsaken all over the world, and we all always knew where the Cappadocians were headed), nothing seems to really unite them. Again I think this issue, while important, is relatively easily solved by pondering what their actual purpose is (beyond hunting ghosts) and who (or what) they keep pissing off to the point where it cuts their numbers in half. Cthonic gods?<br /> <br /> I may be wrong, but I think that most of this results from this being what-I-assume-to-be an early write-up, and later iterations could well fill in the blanks.<br /> In that spirit, as well as for fun, what would you alter, add or subtract from the current write-up of the Council of Bones?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I think that indeed what bothers me the most about them- they feel like hunters who uphold the Vigil and nothing more, which is admirable but feels a bit hollow as they have little to no grasp in the world around them, especially for a conspiracy. For example, if they were allowed to serve as actual mediums and spiritualists, it would have grounded them better into the world IMO- they would have had a stable infrastructure, a source of income and actually not doing anything too bad. By using their talents for personal gain, for example, they would have felt, to me, more human, more flawed, more easy to connect with.<br /> <br /> I also really don't get why they should execute an hunter for using their Endowments before people who are not a part of the Council- other than stopping cross organization games with them, which I don't how common they are in the first place, in a world where many people are touched by the supernatural and conspiracies are known to grant special powers to their agents, killing your members for talking with a ghost before outsiders makes little sense. I mean, even if they were to use their Endowments openly, people who know about the occult would think they are some &quot;regular&quot; mediums, that is, people with Supernatural Merits and such. In the world of hunter, the fact that you can talk with dead people or scry through a mirror is, while not common, not unheard off, and could easily be disguised as something unrelated to the Mark, of which most Council members actually don't know anything.<br /> <br /> I would have also liked if there was some information about their earlier incarnations, like it was in Cheiron and the AO- some Eras where they were in power, as well as some deeper exploration of their infrastructures and their tie ins to the wider world. Like the Golden Age of Islam, or some cultural variations of the past for history development, or that they would actually have some representation as mediums in the wider world- from that old lady who will read your fortune for a couple of coins to that local channel medium who speaks with your dead grandma. The AO have esoteric mysteries and drug dealing. Cheiron have their pharmaceutical juggernaut. The MM have the Catholic Church, and TFV have the american government. Even the Lucifuge and the AKD have a strong infrastructure, from the genealogists of the former to the mystery cults and labyrinths of the later. The Council has some cool things, don't get me wrong- like their initiation rites and such, but it feels more like a loose association which will murder you if you are not acting as they want you to. It feels like you are not getting much from joining them, but have to pay a lot.<br /> <br /> So in short, I think that what bothers me is their seemingly isolation from the world and their almost altruistic devotion for the Vigil. The Wardens of Light were also felt as being &quot;just&quot; an honest and good compact, and I also don't like them by much. Again, other people seems to like them, and my motto is that not every organization is for everyone so I would avoid claiming &quot;that is how I would change them because that way they would have been better&quot;, especially since Hunter is one of the games that encourages you to write your own splats. To each is own, as they say.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-13T15:15:14-08:00","id":1367625,"title":"","content":"IIRC, the Council has the prohibition against showing outsiders their Endownment because they are afraid of being seen in the same vein as L\u00e9s Mysteres and being hunted down to the brink of extinction <b><i>again</i></b>.<br /> <br /> That last part is one of it's more interesting aspects, IMO. They keep getting practically wiped out. Some have pointed out that ghosts could be behind their continual renewal but given how both how their destruction is written and the description of their organizational practices, I'm inclined to disagree.<br /> The dead are what wipes them out frequently; vampires, ghosts, the Bound (not just sin eaters) and possibly even the Arisen are all targets of the Council and sufficient exposure of the Council would result in a terrible backlash. Easily more than enough to wipe out a chapter, and if there is a lead to another chapter, well it just dominos out.<br /> <br /> Survivors can rebuild, adapt the techniques and tricks to they know to their needs, changing some of their methods as they have recreate others whole cloth, hoping it is enough to keep the candle of their dying Vigil alive. At this point, I doubt anyone left in the council has a clue as to the origin of the Mark of the Reaper. Heck, I think the reason their write up is so light on their history is everything prior to the destruction of their immediate predecessor was lost when they fell.<br /> <br /> Elsewhere it has been said that a member of the conspiracy shows up in the Geist Fiction Anthology and it was implied that the 'councillor' did not know/recognise a Sin Eater. Given how long they've been around, that makes no sense unless the Council is ignorant of the history of the dead. They could have been almost anything in ages past, and the modern members would never know.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-13T18:45:47-08:00","id":1367660,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1365834-lostlight-reads-hunter-2e?p=1367625#post1367625\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That last part is one of it's more interesting aspects, IMO. They keep getting practically wiped out. Some have pointed out that ghosts could be behind their continual renewal but given how both how their destruction is written and the description of their organizational practices, I'm inclined to disagree.<br /> The dead are what wipes them out frequently; vampires, ghosts, the Bound (not just sin eaters) and possibly even the Arisen are all targets of the Council and sufficient exposure of the Council would result in a terrible backlash. Easily more than enough to wipe out a chapter, and if there is a lead to another chapter, well it just dominos out.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why not both?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-13T19:43:08-08:00","id":1367673,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1365834-lostlight-reads-hunter-2e?p=1367660#post1367660\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why not both?</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed. No neat boxes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-14T04:15:57-08:00","id":1367722,"title":"","content":"And here comes the time for the next preview! Let's see what things we got for the pseudoscientists and demon spawn!<br /> <br /> *getting flashbacks from all the times I've did scientific interpretation for the CofD*<br /> <br /> I like that the broken way Null Mysteriis is being spelled was given a deeper explanation than &quot;just out of spite&quot;, IIRC.<br /> <br /> I also like how they give a deeper exploration for the history of the group.<br /> <br /> I really like how their fall is being described, only for them to later rise again. Very in theme for the Vigil, and reinforce that playing a member of a collapsed group and reclaiming its place is more than a valid choice. Candles die out only to be ignited again, and the Vigil keeps on growing no matter how hard it falls. Very cool.<br /> <br /> It also serves well to explain their transition from more philosophical and occultic research into the more scientific and modern one.<br /> <br /> Yeah, I by no chance have made a fictional member for the Null Mysteriis from Tel Aviv to serve as an IC way to represent my scientific interpretation of the CofD's setting :P (you'll see it in the STV once spelling check and art will be finished)<br /> <br /> I can only imagine that about half of the compacts' members actually hope that Watt and Fielding are dead, because they want promotion :P<br /> <br /> Yeah, they are very fun to read, while gaining a certain amount of serious treatment that helps them after being treated as the joke of the Hunter society.<br /> <br /> Well, that's one way to make the world into a brighter place- humanity stopped fearing the dark by understanding the gift of fire. If the Null Mysteriis would actually manage to provide a consistent scientific theory for the supernatural, well- the darkness would not go anywhere, but the fear would. That may actually work- if such theory even exists.<br /> <br /> Yeah, the Null Mysteriis feel much more serious, and I like it.<br /> <br /> Two things about the Cataclysmicists- one, with the sudden rise with monsters everywhere, it is very likely that they are right. Second, avian species which sign a coming doom? Go out of here, Strix, you are drunk!<br /> <br /> Again, I really LOVE how they have actually became serious scientists, while still allowing the more pseudoscientists as a part of the Open Minded. <br /> <br /> Wasn't there a thing in C&amp;C about the leader of the Rationalists and the Open Minds making plans to kill one another? I need to double check.<br /> <br /> While the art is less evocative, the scene itself is cool.<br /> <br /> Wicked.<br /> <br /> Very Wicked.<br /> <br /> Oh God Thank You that the Lady is still here. I was absolutely TERRIFIED she would have been killed in order to bring the conspiracy into chaos.<br /> <br /> Lucifuer is the patriarch, and the Lady is the matriarch, and the whole conspiracy are one big happy family! :P<br /> <br /> Shouldn't it have been &quot;Belial&quot;? Like, I know that the 2e Brood is no longer satanist, but I can't think of some covenant, clan or bloodline with infernal ties which is connected to Baal of all demons..<br /> <br /> So yeah, not all Lucifuge just accept the traditional infernal view of their conspiracy after they bump into enough demons in the night.<br /> <br /> The fact that angels outright hates them, and it is hard for me to imagine why a qashmal would hunt the Lucifuge who try to change themselves, I assume that the God Machine has some good reasons to hate the Seventh Generation (both them as stogmatics, infernals, something else or all of the above could work).<br /> <br /> Infernal Royal Celebrities is the best way that demons could view the Lucifuge in the world!<br /> <br /> I am honesty surprised of no mention of the Otodo as a group that could make the Lucifuge doubt their origin, or the 666 members limitation, which I always found as really cool.<br /> <br /> I'm surprised that the writeup didn't mentioned the plot hook that those Lucifuge who were not found were not found by purpose- either due to some agreement the Lady had with the Blind Men, or because the L'Enfant Diabolique got them first.<br /> <br /> Again, it seems that the writeup tries to bring back the Lucifuge into the more &quot;vague&quot; state before Inferno came, and I can understand it. They would still be infernals in my games, but I understand the choice.<br /> <br /> I like their structure.<br /> <br /> I really like that the Lucifuge still know that they are monsters, and that as such all monsters deserves the right to choose for redemption. Again, monster redeemers are a thing.<br /> <br /> And suddenly I feel that the Lady is actually a reference for an historic person which I have somehow missed through all of those years?<br /> <br /> Ah, yes, Castigation.<br /> <br /> I actually think that the Lucifuge having to sacrifice their own blood is a sign of their- and perhaps Lucifer's- redemption. They are actually winning the fight against Hell, and it is awesome.<br /> <br /> I like it that Castigation is addicting.<br /> <br /> Wait- so they ARE infernals??????????????? *happy dance is an happy dance*<br /> <br /> The Will of the Lucifuge is an awesome addition to the game.<br /> <br /> So we no longer have &quot;5 Castigation limit* thing, I assume?<br /> <br /> Ok, overall, the Lucifuge's writeup was AMAZING. The Null Myteriis's was also awesome. Really enjoyed that preview.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-14T12:01:26-08:00","id":1367824,"title":"","content":"I too was very happy with NM being taken seriously. to say I was annoyed by their constant barrage of flanderization in 1st edition is an understatement. I also like that the write-up clarifies the skeptic does not mean &quot;unwilling to believe&quot; but that NM wont accept a claim as true until thoroughly investigated and examined. I was surprised that both Watt and Vincent just disappeared though, I wonder what happened to them. kinda surprised the Open Minds became the smallest faction, but it made sense (but damn is their theory on Vincent weird even for them)<br /> <br /> especially pleased with the Lucifuge, it even answered how the Lucifuge herself keeps her hunters in line. really love the Mark of the Lucifuge condition.<br /> <br /> I will say, I do hope we get more information on the Philosophies of the Lucifuge. the Reconciliation has always been of interest to me. and will admit. I do prefer the old lucifuge artwork","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24173,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","user":"Primordial newcomer","date":". 02-14-2020, 03:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-14T12:18:59-08:00","id":1367829,"title":"","content":"Yeah, the Rationalists came off as trying to cling too hard to a sane world previously. Now they strike me as &quot;no skeptics like stage magicians&quot;; they are honestly enthralled by how weird and wonderful the world is, but take an extremely low view of people who put misleading information into it. Also, the Open Minds come off as the soft sciences in a hard science compact, which fits a lot better than the Token Believers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-14T12:52:38-08:00","id":1367834,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1365834-lostlight-reads-hunter-2e?p=1367829#post1367829\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, the Rationalists came off as trying to cling too hard to a sane world previously. Now they strike me as &amp;quot;no skeptics like stage magicians&amp;quot;; they are honestly enthralled by how weird and wonderful the world is, but take an extremely low view of people who put misleading information into it. Also, the Open Minds come off as the soft sciences in a hard science compact, which fits a lot better than the Token Believers.</div> </div> </div> </div>when we get the tending the flame companion, I'm really hoping for a good writeup on the Open Minds. it's pretty hard to nail that many are genuinely intelligent people who just happen to be into soft sciences (hard for me to find the balance between &quot;smart scientist&quot; and &quot;fringe believer&quot;)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-14T12:57:46-08:00","id":1367837,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1365834-lostlight-reads-hunter-2e?p=1367390#post1367390\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> to be honest, I never understood how being funded by monsters was such a huge deal breaker to so many people. like sure, they can influence TFV with taking some funding away, but they are largely unaware of just about everything else</div> </div> </div> </div>If TFV is being funded by monsters, they\u2019re not sitting distantly handing them money. If it\u2019s vampires, they\u2019ve stacked the Steering Committee with ghouls, if it\u2019s Seers of the Throne they\u2019ve stacked it with Profane Urim thralls, etc etc.<br /> <br /> But the idea TFV needed secret outside funding like the US gov doesn\u2019t have a black budget, and disappearing billions in Iraq, etc etc, was dumb.<br /> <br /> But anyway, the difference for the Council is the rank and file know they\u2019re taking the guidance of ghosts and drawing on them for power, while something like TFV is a mystery hidden from the rank and file, much less other Conspiracies (if that plot hook is even being repeated at all)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 02-14-2020, 04:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-14T13:00:38-08:00","id":1367838,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1365834-lostlight-reads-hunter-2e?p=1367834#post1367834\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> when we get the tending the flame companion, I'm really hoping for a good writeup on the Open Minds. it's pretty hard to nail that many are genuinely intelligent people who just happen to be into soft sciences (hard for me to find the balance between &amp;quot;smart scientist&amp;quot; and &amp;quot;fringe believer&amp;quot<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>You guys do realize the term \u201csoft sciences\u201d refers to the social sciences, not pseudoscience, right? Or are you intending to say you don\u2019t see why intelligent people would be into sociology, psychology, etc?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-14T13:21:47-08:00","id":1367845,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1365834-lostlight-reads-hunter-2e?p=1367838#post1367838\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You guys do realize the term \u201csoft sciences\u201d refers to the social sciences, not pseudoscience, right? Or are you intending to say you don\u2019t see why intelligent people would be into sociology, psychology, etc?</div> </div> </div> </div>oops, my bad lol. &quot;fringe sciences&quot; I mean. I genuinely forgot soft science means psychology and such (actually have played with a friend who was an NM sociologist by the way)<br /> <br /> anyway, concerning TFV, while vampires do tend to make their influences deep, to say they have what is basically entire control of the conspiracy is a huge stretch. if they really did, they wouldnt need to worry about threatening to pull funding when TFV defies what they want","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-14T15:38:17-08:00","id":1367896,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1365834-lostlight-reads-hunter-2e?p=1367837#post1367837\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If TFV is being funded by monsters, they\u2019re not sitting distantly handing them money. If it\u2019s vampires, they\u2019ve stacked the Steering Committee with ghouls, if it\u2019s Seers of the Throne they\u2019ve stacked it with Profane Urim thralls, etc etc.<br /> <br /> But the idea TFV needed secret outside funding like the US gov doesn\u2019t have a black budget, and disappearing billions in Iraq, etc etc, was dumb.<br /> <br /> But anyway, the difference for the Council is the rank and file know they\u2019re taking the guidance of ghosts and drawing on them for power, while something like TFV is a mystery hidden from the rank and file, much less other Conspiracies (if that plot hook is even being repeated at all)</div> </div> </div> </div>It's something I never understood with Vampires being in secret control of TFV. In the Vampire line, Vampire exert a lot of control at the local level but almost none at the state or national level. VTR doesn't have a global org. like the Camarilla to control all of vampire society. So even if vampires controlled TFV and they used it to wipe out their rivals, then TFV would really only be killing vampires in one or two cities because if those Vampires controlling TFV had that much power they would be basically the Camarilla.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24179-grimmi05","name":"Grimmi05","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-14T15:49:12-08:00","id":1367899,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grimmi05</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1365834-lostlight-reads-hunter-2e?p=1367896#post1367896\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's something I never understood with Vampires being in secret control of TFV. In the Vampire line, Vampire exert a lot of control at the local level but almost none at the state or national level. VTR doesn't have a global org. like the Camarilla to control all of vampire society. So even if vampires controlled TFV and they used it to wipe out their rivals, then TFV would really only be killing vampires in one or two cities because if those Vampires controlling TFV had that much power they would be basically the Camarilla.</div> </div> </div> </div>that's why it's only funding in my mind. they have very limited control. if they really had ghouls implanted at the the upper reaches, they would never have to worry about hunters getting orders (and they would focus exclusively on vampires. why would they care about threats that dont concern them?)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-14T16:13:18-08:00","id":1367907,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grimmi05</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1365834-lostlight-reads-hunter-2e?p=1367896#post1367896\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's something I never understood with Vampires being in secret control of TFV. In the Vampire line, Vampire exert a lot of control at the local level but almost none at the state or national level. VTR doesn't have a global org. like the Camarilla to control all of vampire society. So even if vampires controlled TFV and they used it to wipe out their rivals, then TFV would really only be killing vampires in one or two cities because if those Vampires controlling TFV had that much power they would be basically the Camarilla.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why a) would the US government need outside funding for black ops?<br /> <br /> b) would vampires fund operations they don\u2019t control? I would think the only reason they\u2019d do it is if they could direct it, as 1e described.<br /> <br /> <br /> AT MY OWN TABLE - neither vampires or any other supernatural faction fund or control VALKYRIE. TFV\u2019s dark secret is the deals they\u2019ve made to support the power of supernaturals who assert stability and the status-quo over their communities. They\u2019re allowing Invictus, Seer, etc predation in the interest of stability, but it\u2019s humans who have made that decision.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-14T16:28:12-08:00","id":1367910,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1365834-lostlight-reads-hunter-2e?p=1367899#post1367899\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> that's why it's only funding in my mind. they have very limited control. if they really had ghouls implanted at the the upper reaches, they would never have to worry about hunters getting orders (and they would focus exclusively on vampires. why would they care about threats that dont concern them?)</div> </div> </div> </div>Even funding really doesn't make sense to me. maybe if it was like 5 or 6 vampires pooling all of their resources together. then maybe TFV could have a budget of yes. but once again it leads into the whole if those vampires have that much money, power, and influence how come they aren't Cam. 2.0?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24179-grimmi05","name":"Grimmi05","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-14T16:30:59-08:00","id":1367912,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1365834-lostlight-reads-hunter-2e?p=1367907#post1367907\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why a) would the US government need outside funding for black ops?<br /> <br /> b) would vampires fund operations they don\u2019t control? I would think the only reason they\u2019d do it is if they could direct it, as 1e described.<br /> <br /> <br /> AT MY OWN TABLE - neither vampires or any other supernatural faction fund or control VALKYRIE. TFV\u2019s dark secret is the deals they\u2019ve made to support the power of supernaturals who assert stability and the status-quo over their communities. They\u2019re allowing Invictus, Seer, etc predation in the interest of stability, but it\u2019s humans who have made that decision.</div> </div> </div> </div>That makes much more sense. I run TFV as they allow those groups to do those things because A. it protects the status quo and B. it would cost so much more money trying to root out and extremainate that many creatures that have human intelligence and can fight back. So the deal is 'Don't make waves because we know where you and yours live.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24179-grimmi05","name":"Grimmi05","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-14T16:34:14-08:00","id":1367914,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1365834-lostlight-reads-hunter-2e?p=1367722#post1367722\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait- so they ARE infernals??????????????? *happy dance is an happy dance*</div> </div> </div> </div>I am obliged to cut a hair here and point out that what has happened is that we have a single origin source for the Lucifuge with discernable names and an association with A hell. It is not EXPLICITLY tying the Lucifuge to the Inferno.<br /> <br /> Now with that said, I'll admit that's splitting hairs-looks like a duck, quacks like a duck, spreads sin and hellfire like a duck, must be a duck-but the demon, demon, demon, demon, or demon problem is pervasive enough that even toeing right up to the line, a notice of not crossing it must at least be given due.<br /> <br /> Also I don't like it, but that's my issue.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-14T20:35:24-08:00","id":1367964,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar503_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"503\" data-vbnamecard=\"503\">LostLight</a>, I have a question concerning the Lucifuge if that's fine. do you think it's safe to say the Hunters are, in a manner of speaking, spiritually enslaved? I mean, I know many conspiracies keep their members under tight watch, but they normally get benefits from it. the Lucifuge hunters dont, it seems, and instead get almost mystically compelled to follow commands when they do get them. <br /> <br /> I'm not saying that makes the Lucifuge herself super evil, but spiritually enslaving her hunters seems pretty bad (I assume she is also aware of what they do, being why she knows about the ones that try to escape)<br /> <br /> also, cant freaking wait for MM, hope Baudolino is still alive","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-14T20:36:18-08:00","id":1367965,"title":"","content":"It's just idea I read it here, but really, making <i>Task Force: VALKYRIE</i> project of <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/the-cryptocracy-contagion-chronicle/\" target=\"_blank\">Cryptocracy Faction</a> council has ssssoooo much sense in <b>CoD</b> universe. Remembering those that do not know, Cryptocracy is Contagion reaction crossover group that supports stability of humanity and it's rules, implying that chaos leads to next strains of Contagion. Those are all monsters that wants to have stability, order and to rule of humanity. It's much more fractured from Camarilla of Vampire of old, but it's the closest we have to it. Invictus are natural members, just like Seers, Guardians or even Silver Ladder, from Mage. As it's cross faction alliance fighting unnatural sickness of the world, it has more the reasons, pull and motives to create TFV compared to Invictus alone.<br /> <br /> With TFV folding in it's self the Barret Comission and Division 6, it has even more reason to do so. Especially as Division 6 is Seers produced group that in 2E <b>HtV</b> is canonically now part of TFV, so crossovers of various government sanction monsters is already in line.<br /> <br /> I really think that whole <b>HtV</b> gameline will blossom from this idea alone. I will start a topic on this one. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> EDIT: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1367967-2e-task-force-valkyrie-as-cryptocracy-project\">Seperate topic is here</a> - interesting if it will take many people on board with idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 02-15-2020, 12:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-14T20:49:51-08:00","id":1367968,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1365834-lostlight-reads-hunter-2e?p=1367965#post1367965\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's just idea I read it here, but really, making <i>Task Force: VALKYRIE</i> project of <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">http://theonyxpath.com/the-cryptocracy-contagion-chronicle/&amp;quot;]Cryptocracy</a> Faction[/URL] council has ssssoooo much sense in <b>CoD</b> universe. Remembering those that do not know, Cryptocracy is Contagion reaction crossover group that supports stability of humanity and it's rules, implying that chaos leads to next strains of Contagion. Those are all monsters that wants to have stability, order and to rule of humanity. It's much more fractured from Camarilla of Vampire of old, but it's the closest we have to it. Invictus are natural members, just like Seers, Guardians or even Silver Ladder, from Mage. As it's cross faction alliance fighting unnatural sickness of the world, it has more the reasons, pull and motives to create TFV compared to Invictus alone.<br /> <br /> With TFV folding in it's self the Barret Comission and Division 6, it has even more reason to do so. Especially as Division 6 is Seers produced group that in 2E <b>HtV</b> is canonically now part of TFV, so crossovers of various government sanction monsters is already in line. <br /> <br /> I really think that whole <b>HtV</b> gameline will blossom from this idea alone. I will start a topic on this one. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah that was me talking about my \u201cVALKYRIE\u2019s made devil\u2019s bargains to maintain order with pro-status-quo supernaturals\u201d pitch.<br /> <br /> <br /> One option I really like this opens up is you can actually define a distinct role of the Barrett Commission that not only stops them being redundant with TFV, but puts them at firm cross purposes. Barrett Commission is largely about trying to cleans the halls of power of supernatural manipulators. But that\u2019s many of the same groups that the VALKYRIE Steering Committee has made deals with, and the Barrett Commission\u2019s efforts risk throwing the balance of power into chaos.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-14T21:38:38-08:00","id":1367975,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1365834-lostlight-reads-hunter-2e?p=1367964#post1367964\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar503_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"503\" data-vbnamecard=\"503\">LostLight</a>, I have a question concerning the Lucifuge if that's fine. do you think it's safe to say the Hunters are, in a manner of speaking, spiritually enslaved? I mean, I know many conspiracies keep their members under tight watch, but they normally get benefits from it. the Lucifuge hunters dont, it seems, and instead get almost mystically compelled to follow commands when they do get them.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying that makes the Lucifuge herself super evil, but spiritually enslaving her hunters seems pretty bad (I assume she is also aware of what they do, being why she knows about the ones that try to escape)<br /> <br /> also, cant freaking wait for MM, hope Baudolino is still alive</div> </div> </div> </div>See &quot;Operate under Probable-Metaphysical Gunpoint of a Woman of Indeterminate Origin(Lucifuge)&quot;.<br /> <br /> Lady Lucifuge is a person who deals with Evil on a scale that is about as Real as it can exist, and to Some Degree is reliant upon such Real Power of Evil for her response.<br /> <br /> Said response is unlikely to be....Pick the words that make you comfortable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 02-15-2020, 01:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-14T22:27:09-08:00","id":1367988,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1365834-lostlight-reads-hunter-2e?p=1367975#post1367975\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">See &quot;Operate under Probable-Metaphysical Gunpoint of a Woman of Indeterminate Origin(Lucifuge)&quot;.<br /> <br /> Lady Lucifuge is a person who deals with Evil on a scale that is about as Real as it can exist, and to Some Degree is reliant upon such Real Power of Evil for her response.<br /> <br /> Said response is unlikely to be....Pick the words that make you comfortable.</div> </div> </div> </div>To speak to this:<br /> <br /> Back around the time that Mortal Remains was coming out somebody made a complaint that the Lucifuge's take on Sin-Eaters confirmed the Bound were delusional because none of the figures krewe mythos dealt with matched any of their records of angels and demons.<br /> <br /> You can probably imagine how much more of a laugh that assertion became after my focused reread of Hunter 1e included, specifically, &quot;a lot of the agents of the Lucifuge are explicitly brainwashed.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-14T22:43:53-08:00","id":1367991,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1365834-lostlight-reads-hunter-2e?p=1367988#post1367988\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To speak to this:<br /> <br /> Back around the time that Mortal Remains was coming out somebody made a complaint that the Lucifuge's take on Sin-Eaters confirmed the Bound were delusional because none of the figures krewe mythos dealt with matched any of their records of angels and demons.<br /> <br /> You can probably imagine how much more of a laugh that assertion became after my focused reread of Hunter 1e included, specifically, &quot;a lot of the agents of the Lucifuge are explicitly brainwashed.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>There is a reason &quot;Welcome to Hunter, You're not the good guys.&quot; is a refrain of mine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-14T23:20:40-08:00","id":1367996,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1365834-lostlight-reads-hunter-2e?p=1367991#post1367991\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is a reason &quot;Welcome to Hunter, You're not the good guys.&quot; is a refrain of mine.</div> </div> </div> </div>Frankly, I'm very much in the two-guns-and-a-square-jaw mode of the vigil, but &quot;you're not the good guys, but better than the bad guys&quot; is why I like hunters, really. And given the Lucifuge is a lady from the Dark Ages who, as noted, knows perfectly well her relatives have a genetic code that actively tempts them to the dark side - yeah, her tendency to indoctrinate the reluctant by force barely registers as that evil in comparison. By her time's standards, it's probably not especially amoral either, she's saving souls from the Adversary in return for vassalage, like any moronic baron would do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-14T23:27:05-08:00","id":1367998,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1365834-lostlight-reads-hunter-2e?p=1367996#post1367996\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And given the Lucifuge is a lady from the Dark Ages who, as noted, knows perfectly well her relatives have a genetic code that actively tempts them to the dark side - yeah, her tendency to indoctrinate the reluctant by force barely registers as that evil in comparison.</div> </div> </div> </div>Lord knows she's not the only one making use of that part of the toolkit \u2014 I'm eager to see if/how 2e adapts the &quot;deprogram the occult mental influence out of someone&quot; Tactic that absolutely everybody more organized than two dozen goobers with camcorders and Glocks got a cost break to learn.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-15T01:47:44-08:00","id":1368010,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1365834-lostlight-reads-hunter-2e?p=1367914#post1367914\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am obliged to cut a hair here and point out that what has happened is that we have a single origin source for the Lucifuge with discernable names and an association with A hell. It is not EXPLICITLY tying the Lucifuge to the Inferno.<br /> <br /> Now with that said, I'll admit that's splitting hairs-looks like a duck, quacks like a duck, spreads sin and hellfire like a duck, must be a duck-but the demon, demon, demon, demon, or demon problem is pervasive enough that even toeing right up to the line, a notice of not crossing it must at least be given due.<br /> <br /> Also I don't like it, but that's my issue.</div> </div> </div> </div>I get where you are coming from, and I agree with you- the book does not explicitly states that the Lucifuge are infernals in origin. It states that Castigation only affects does monsters which has the Infernal Dread Power, which is indeed a bit more defined that 1e's version, but until we would actually see the Dread Power in question we don't really know what it means. <br /> <br /> In general, my view is that if your are playing a Lucifuge member, the basic assumption is that the Devil exists. With Inferno being a thing in the CofD, the easiest answer would be that the Lucifuge are infernal in origin. It is similar to the idea if in a game involving the Sanctified, it is likely that God does indeed exist (even if He is not as nice as some people want you to think). Heck, the Devil could indeed be the symbolic source of all monsters, more of the Dark Mother than the head of Hell's legions. But as an Inferno fan, I, of course, easily take the infernal option, but I don't think that the way that 2e is written outright invalidates some other views of the Lucifuge, at least by what is known.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-15T02:05:16-08:00","id":1368011,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1365834-lostlight-reads-hunter-2e?p=1367964#post1367964\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar503_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"503\" data-vbnamecard=\"503\">LostLight</a>, I have a question concerning the Lucifuge if that's fine. do you think it's safe to say the Hunters are, in a manner of speaking, spiritually enslaved? I mean, I know many conspiracies keep their members under tight watch, but they normally get benefits from it. the Lucifuge hunters dont, it seems, and instead get almost mystically compelled to follow commands when they do get them.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying that makes the Lucifuge herself super evil, but spiritually enslaving her hunters seems pretty bad (I assume she is also aware of what they do, being why she knows about the ones that try to escape)</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, you could indeed call it &quot;enslavement&quot;- but aren't we all slaves to our world and nature? :P<br /> <br /> A bit more seriously, some Lucifuge agents are indeed brainwashed to go against their dark nature. Notice that the Lucifuge are aware that they do so- they don't try to sugarcoat it. A free Lucifuge member is dangerous, and while Hell never enslaves you, it does cheers for you as you fall into corruption. And not all members of the Lucifuge are brainwashed- many choose to fight evil and go against their nature. <br /> <br /> Now, the Will of the Lucifuge is indeed a small part of the Lady's will which creeps into your mind and soul, and compels you to follow her orders- but notice that it is for those members which are in good standing with the organization. The Lucifuge is, indeed, the organization, and she lives in her children. You can leave (well, you can try at least), and then the Condition is resolved- but what would be your other option? Falling prey to demons who treat you like royalty until you fuck up the world?<br /> <br /> You can serve in heaven or rule in hell. You either submit yourself to save the world or do as you wish. The demons come and whisper to you, promising you freedom, and how great and amazing you could be. It is easy to fall into temptation, easy to run wild in Hell and be loved and adored as you fuck up everything you once cared about. Hell doesn't takes your free will- and that's the beauty of it. You choose your own damnation, and when you fall kicking and screaming to meet your parents, you will know that you have done exactly what they wanted you to do, and they are so proud of you and you have no one to blame but yourself.<br /> <br /> So yeah, you enslave yourself to the Lucifuge, both organization and a person. But it is a choice- well, usually. The other choice would have been to get killed, perhaps, or maybe they brainwashed you into making that choice. The other option would be letting you to roam free and bring hell upon earth. We are all slaves to our choices- and there is no freedom in hell, just understanding that you became a slave to your sins, and chains worn from free will while the Devil laughs in your face.<br /> <br /> At least, that's what the Lucifuge tells themselves to sleep at night.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> also, cant freaking wait for MM, hope Baudolino is still alive </div> </div> </div>Me too! His dinners with the Lady is one of my favorite plot hooks for Hunter :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-15T07:21:29-08:00","id":1368039,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1365834-lostlight-reads-hunter-2e?p=1367996#post1367996\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Frankly, I'm very much in the two-guns-and-a-square-jaw mode of the vigil, but &quot;you're not the good guys, but better than the bad guys&quot; is why I like hunters, really.</div> </div> </div> </div>The best part about this is that Hunter responds to both our takes with &quot;Why not both?&quot;<br /> <br /> Maybe more so with the Knights of Saint Adrian, but in general.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-15T20:27:05-08:00","id":1368219,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar503_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"503\" data-vbnamecard=\"503\">LostLight</a>. your whole response is an incredibly convincing argument that the Lucifuge herself is right in what she does. I also wont lie, the Mark adds yet another mystery for the Truth to investigate, and I like that (I know it's really the storytellers fun to make mysteries, and I have never played as a Truth Lucifuge yet, but having stuff like the mark and the vampire paintings from Night Stalkers is just great for the faction)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-17T05:58:56-08:00","id":1368517,"title":"","content":"And time to review one of the new compacts and our old and loved church hounds!<br /> <br /> Again, full disclosure, the Abbey was my favorite compact so I may be too critical towards SWORN. On the other hand, as I am not American, much of the cultural reference towards SWORN would be lost to me. I do hope I'll like them, but I'll do my best to try and read them from the point of someone who didn't feel included culturally wise, and that it answers their way to connect to the game. Can't promise that I would like them, but I'll try to be as neutral as possible.<br /> <br /> And here we go!<br /> <br /> SWORN- Well, it at least defines the acronym. <br /> <br /> Ok, so some events that I have somewhat heard of but was never very familiar with. At the very least, I would learn something about american history in here.<br /> <br /> Feels somewhat Union like, well as much as the Night Watch felt Union like.<br /> <br /> I must say that it feels much more like the 1e style of writeups, where the compact was very focused around a specific case which founded it. Not that it is a bad thing, of course- especially for a new compact.<br /> <br /> While I would have liked a Keepers of the Weave reference (or even Wardens of Light), but at the very least it describes why there isn't- those traditions were lost with the Relocation. People being stuck out of place and their culture broken apart is indeed a tragedy from which compacts rise. The whole world is in chaos, and candles are being lite to guide them through the darkness.<br /> <br /> I personally think they could have left out the overly detailed cell structure, but it does not harm the writeup or anything.<br /> <br /> While I get the focus around the foundation of the compact, I would have liked it if the writeup would have focused more about who SWORN are beside being a compact for Native Americans- you know, what that differs them from any other cell of Native American hunters.<br /> <br /> I do like the Enemy section, which actually gives some more character to the group. Their division between &quot;natural&quot; and &quot;intelligent&quot;, as well as &quot;invasive&quot; and &quot;hybrid&quot; monsters gives some interesting twist towards how they operate their Vigil.<br /> <br /> I think that the main issue with having a cultural specific group in the core is that it somewhat limits who you can play in the organization towards a certain ethnicity. Again, I am not saying that those groups should not exist, but they make more sense to me as things you gain in supplements about specific regions and such. I mean, I can play a Native American who is a part of the Null Mysteriis, for example, but you can't really play a Jew who is a part of SWORN, for example. On the other hand, I am not sure how well you can play a Native American who is a part of the Union, and I am definitely sure you can't play a Muslim who is a part of the Long Night, so what we think as a mainstream is heavily tilted by our own culture. However, there are Christians all around the world while Native Americans are found only in, well, the Americas. But most of the people who fund the Kickstarter seems to be from the US, so... Yeah, there is no right or wrong in this subject, but if it helps some people who love Hunter to feel included then why not?<br /> <br /> Ammm- the Unyielding Hearts Society actually helps SWORN feels more global in terms of focusing less about the circumstances for SWORN's creation and more about how their classifications and more &quot;ecological&quot; view of the Vigil. I think I would have liked it if the writeup were to focus more about that part of the compact and less on the specific death which brought it into existence, like how the Null Mysteriis's talk about the group's founder and focus more on their views and ideologies. A compact which is all about &quot;protecting Native Americans&quot; feels a bit too niche for a core, IMO. A compact which is about preserving the natural order which was lost due colonialism and the lose of ancient traditions is something I could connect to.<br /> <br /> In general the Factions actually enrich the writeup in a few levels, presenting both the more militant and the more open faces of SWORN- and reinforced that no, you are not the good guys.<br /> <br /> Fighting nun art is awesome.<br /> <br /> Yep, the Inquisition is here.<br /> <br /> Seems that the MM now has a strong focus around witches. Interesting.<br /> <br /> Ah- here is the vampire hunting part.<br /> <br /> Now, that's actually really cool! I remember that some people complained about why the MM were given that name when they hunt for vampire instead of witches, and the writeup now gives a very good reason, IMO.<br /> <br /> So traditions versus the need to change. I wonder if that means that the day for them absorbing the Long Night is closer than ever- I mean, if those suspicious bastards would stop thinking that the Catholic Church is the devil :P<br /> <br /> Baudolino is still alive! Great!<br /> <br /> And he still have his dinners with the Lucifuge <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> OVerall, I like their Enemy section.<br /> <br /> So the Orders are unofficial? I was sure that those divisions were intended by the organization.<br /> <br /> I'm surprised that there was no tension between the orders as it was presented in C&amp;C.<br /> <br /> So they are still rigid Catholics, Endowments wise- now I wonder how it works with them trying to share knowledge and resources through other religious groups.<br /> <br /> The fact that Benediction requires you a connection to the Pope (meaning, Baudolino) in order to work is an interesting plot hook. I mean, if you are a good Christian, you can just handwave it by saying that God exists. Otherwise- the requirement to be a part of a large infrastructure to preform miracles kinds leads towards the wrong God...<br /> <br /> So it seems they have scrapped the Saints Calendar for a more simple Integrity dependence system- healthy mind leads to healthy spirit. The fact the Theban Sorcery operates in a similar way does rise some red flags- no wonder that Baudolino tells no one about the Lance.<br /> <br /> Yep, the whole thing stinks from Theban Sorcery- but as Benedictions are not related to Vitae (and to be fair, so does Theban Sorcery), what exactly powers it? Heck, what exactly powers Theban Sorcery? The God Machine? The Judges? God Himself? How does Baudolino maintains that ability to grant someone the blessing of Benediction by serving as a divine channel for SOMETHING? <br /> <br /> Again, notice that up until now, every Endowment requires some sort of spiritual metamorphosis to work- the AO need to learn how to transform poison to Elixirs. Cheiron needs monster parts to be transplanted into them. The Council marks with with the sign of Death. The Lucifuge are born this way. And now the MM must be blessed by the Pope and commit themselves to the conspiracy. Gaining Endowment changes something in the Hunter- my personal view is that it serves as a &quot;stabilized Divergence&quot;, something which does not crack your soul, but perhaps leaves a scar upon it. That is, every Endowment once started from a Divergence, but if the method becomes stable and reliable enough it turns into Endowments. Again, just my personal theory on the subject- and we are still wondering how Advanced Armory will work with this (they do have that chip inside of them, however).<br /> <br /> Yeah, that's basically Theban Sorcery for mortals.. Damn it, what if the Lance is actually right and there is a God out there in the CofD, who is just not very nice? <br /> <br /> And they can still bring people back to life! Exactly what I wanted from Hunter- to mess up with everything other supernaturals know about the world :P (I wonder what would happen if they would try to revive someone just as they are being Embraced..)<br /> <br /> And again we see the rogue cells are a HUGE problem for conspiracies. I have some very interesting plans for the Order of St Jude, and they tie well with that plot hook about those hunters who hunt for &quot;non righteous hunters&quot;..<br /> <br /> Overall, I really liked the MM's writeup, and I found SWORN more interesting than I expected them to be. Only two more previews to go before we can finally go deep into the next chapters of Hunter!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-17T08:36:13-08:00","id":1368536,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1365834-lostlight-reads-hunter-2e?p=1368517#post1368517\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A compact which is all about &quot;protecting Native Americans&quot; feels a bit too niche for a core, IMO. A compact which is about preserving the natural order which was lost due colonialism and the lose of ancient traditions is something I could connect to.<br /> <br /> In general the Factions actually enrich the writeup in a few levels, presenting both the more militant and the more open faces of SWORN- and reinforced that no, you are not the good guys.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would also liked more if the opening description of the SWORN in last paragraph pointed that now they are including other forgotten tradition around the world. It would make it much more fitting for the core from straight forward.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1365834-lostlight-reads-hunter-2e?p=1368517#post1368517\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yep, the Inquisition is here.<br /> <br /> Seems that the MM now has a strong focus around witches. Interesting.<br /> <br /> Ah- here is the vampire hunting part.<br /> <br /> Now, that's actually really cool! I remember that some people complained about why the MM were given that name when they hunt for vampire instead of witches, and the writeup now gives a very good reason, IMO.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is it me, or did writers moved MM creation from about 50 years after printing the book - to only few years after it? Pointing that half century later it was official papal decree and before those were unofficial witch hunters?<br /> <br /> I still do not see the reason why MM is called this way and they still hunt vampires. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ( Beside 'they boss is previous ghoul' ) Conspiracy is called 'Hammer on Witches', for Popes sake! ( Vampires relation are still not open to this. )<br /> <br /> Also - I would much more prefer if 1st dot of MM Status give you to choose where to allocate Specialty - vampire, witches and demons, perhaps. Especially, as we have pointed at least two Orders inside conspiracy that hunt vampire and witches, specifically.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 02-17-2020, 11:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-17T08:49:27-08:00","id":1368537,"title":"","content":"personally, I dont feel Benedictions needing a blessing means the god machine is involved. the catholic church, and I do know since I'm Catholic, is an institution that wont just accept you as Catholic. you must prove yourself and then be formally inducted in. it makes sense Benedictions are the same way (plus, if Lucifuge tilts toward Satan being real, so should MM toward God). though, they do seem more like Theban sorcery than ever. personally I will be keeping the saints day bonuses.<br /> <br /> the SWORN has redeemed itself in my eyes. by far the best &quot;Enemy&quot; section in my opinion. i will admit, i was surprised by their militant faction, considering SWORN was partially founded by a lesbian","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-17T08:51:25-08:00","id":1368538,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1365834-lostlight-reads-hunter-2e?p=1368536#post1368536\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it me, or did writers moved MM creation from about 50 years after printing the book - to only few years after it? Pointing that half century later it was official papal decree and before those were unofficial witch hunters?</div> </div> </div> </div>The book from which the conspiracy takes its name was condemned as heretical a few years after it was published, which is consistent with 1e's writeup, as is the eighty-year span between the book's publication and the creation of the conspiracy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-17T09:12:53-08:00","id":1368542,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1365834-lostlight-reads-hunter-2e?p=1368537#post1368537\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">personally, I dont feel Benedictions needing a blessing means the god machine is involved. the catholic church, and I do know since I'm Catholic, is an institution that wont just accept you as Catholic. you must prove yourself and then be formally inducted in. it makes sense Benedictions are the same way (plus, if Lucifuge tilts toward Satan being real, so should MM toward God). though, they do seem more like Theban sorcery than ever. personally I will be keeping the saints day bonuses.</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't said it was the God Machine as much as I said it means a connection to <i>something</i>, as the Pope/Baudolino serves as a channel for an higher power. It may be God. It may be something else. Like, Rose once said that in Vampire, God should be real and He granted Theban Sorcery to the Lance. She also said that she thinks that the God Machine could be a good source for Theban Sorcery, while Dave said that in his headcanon, those are Utterances (hence connection to the Judges). In Hunter, God could, without doubt, exist, and serve as the power behind Benedictions. But if Theban Sorcery is similar to Benediction, and the God Machine, the Judges, the Father, the Principle and (literally) God knows what else could serve as its source, Benediction could just as easily be connected to any divine power- including God Himself. <br /> <br /> Again, I am not saying it is not God- but the &quot;anti pope&quot; found his own way to grant Benediction, which means that either God has more than one channel for power through the Catholic Church or that things are much more murky than we think.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-17T10:35:08-08:00","id":1368566,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1365834-lostlight-reads-hunter-2e?p=1368542#post1368542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I didn't said it was the God Machine as much as I said it means a connection to <i>something</i>, as the Pope/Baudolino serves as a channel for an higher power. It may be God. It may be something else. Like, Rose once said that in Vampire, God should be real and He granted Theban Sorcery to the Lance. She also said that she thinks that the God Machine could be a good source for Theban Sorcery, while Dave said that in his headcanon, those are Utterances (hence connection to the Judges). In Hunter, God could, without doubt, exist, and serve as the power behind Benedictions. But if Theban Sorcery is similar to Benediction, and the God Machine, the Judges, the Father, the Principle and (literally) God knows what else could serve as its source, Benediction could just as easily be connected to any divine power- including God Himself. <br /> <br /> Again, I am not saying it is not God- but the &quot;anti pope&quot; found his own way to grant Benediction, which means that either God has more than one channel for power through the Catholic Church or that things are much more murky than we think.</div> </div> </div> </div>ohhh lol. ok, I really thought you just meant &quot;it must be the god machine&quot; when you the wrong god. my bad. <br /> <br /> if it's ok, I do have a question. do you think more should be done to characterize the militant sub factions? what I mean is make them less one note, like how Athanasius just seems like a group hardliners and nothing else (admittedly I do have a problem with how many militant sub factions seem to just serve as the &quot;hunter organization gone wrong&quot;. perhaps Tending the flame could help). speaking of which, how do you feel about free specialties being taken away (and the 3 dot status effect for MM. That one seems kinda dumb in my mind)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-17T11:21:36-08:00","id":1368585,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1365834-lostlight-reads-hunter-2e?p=1368536#post1368536\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I still do not see the reason why MM is called this way and they still hunt vampires. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ( Beside 'they boss is previous ghoul' ) Conspiracy is called 'Hammer on Witches', for Popes sake! ( Vampires relation are still not open to this. ).</div> </div> </div> </div>Because Baudolino used the witch paranoia as a tool to motivate the Church to hunt vampires. His claims were that all the things you think that witches are doing are in fact the actions of vampires, and he utilized the already existing christian hunters which were driven by the fear from witches and directed their actions to something which was more useful. From his point of view, vampires are the main source of evil in the world, and as the voice whispering in the Pope's hear, he constructed the organization to fit his own zeal and hate towards those who abused him. <br /> <br /> So the MM use their name because when they were founded, they were built upon the witch paranoia, and Baudolino told them that what they think is witches was actually vampires. It is even possible that he didn't knew about witches at the time, and believed that vampires are the actual source of the claims- he knew that vampires were realm, and thought them to be the source of the claims about witches while innocents suffer. IIRC, the Catholic Church actually viewed the belief in witches as heresy, so claiming that someone was a witch could have ended up with your getting the stake. Vampires, on the other hand, were definitely real, and as such it was better to hunt them than some poor women who were just too old or acted weird.<br /> <br /> In short, the MM doesn't gain its name because it hunts witches, but because it was founded on the fear from witches. That was their concept since 1e, and 2e have reinforced it through the writeup and grounded it with history. In modern nights they are hunting witches and demons, but vampires are still their main target because Baudolino is still the power behind the scenes, and he still hates the damn monsters (not to mention that he need to keep his lifespan somehow)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-17T11:25:15-08:00","id":1368588,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1365834-lostlight-reads-hunter-2e?p=1368566#post1368566\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> if it's ok, I do have a question. do you think more should be done to characterize the militant sub factions? what I mean is make them less one note, like how Athanasius just seems like a group hardliners and nothing else (admittedly I do have a problem with how many militant sub factions seem to just serve as the &quot;hunter organization gone wrong&quot;. perhaps Tending the flame could help). speaking of which, how do you feel about free specialties being taken away (and the 3 dot status effect for MM. That one seems kinda dumb in my mind)</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that the writeups do their best with whatever wordcount they have to describe the different factions. Sure, more development for subfactions could have been nice, but if it comes on the expense of the actual conspiracy wirteup it would feel like a waste (again, my main complain about SWORN is that all the cool things about them are found in their subfactions and Enemy section, instead of the body of the text).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-17T11:46:58-08:00","id":1368599,"title":"","content":"In Doubting Souls it gets into some of the origins of the Malleus Maleficarum, and it does seem like Baudolino didn't exactly start out corrupt. They originally hunted vampires and demons, but he thought vampires were too canny to get caught by the witch trials, and sought some help for identifying and hunting them.<br /> <br /> While it's easy to dismiss Ambrogio Baudolino as a corrupt and cackling evil mastermind, it doesn't really indicate that at all. Looking at the witch trials, and aspects of the church itself and the way nations and ideas shift it would be easy to recognize that if you start a group hunting them in the 1500s, it will be gone or shifted in focus by the 1700s. Keeping one person in charge of a conspiracy is an easy way to give reason for that conspiracy lasting more than the lifespan of that person. And sure he can be an evil bastard who adopts all the puppies in Italy just to kick them, he can just as easily be a dude who made a hard choice because he believes the Malleus Maleficarum is objectively bettering the world. I'm not of the mindset, but anyone who's been in the Vampire forum has likely seen people saying things like 'you could get rid of all vampires and the world would be a better place.' Baudolino may believe the same, and think its worth his soul to make it happen.<br /> <br /> My own opinion, I really like the SWORN write-up, but the Malleus write-up is kinda bland, like reading the various MM sections from the books and writing a summary.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 02-17-2020, 02:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-17T12:05:55-08:00","id":1368606,"title":"","content":"I am far from claiming Baudolino as corrupted- I view him as an hunter who does exactly what he thinks is right. He was abused by a vampire, vampires are the true source of all evil, and if he can extend his lifespan by using the blood of his enemies in order to keep on hunting them down what is bad with that?<br /> <br /> Baudolino uphold the Vigil and does the best to protect the world- and if he turns out messy and bloody it is because the Vigil is messy and bloody.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-17T12:28:26-08:00","id":1368616,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1365834-lostlight-reads-hunter-2e?p=1368606#post1368606\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am far from claiming Baudolino as corrupted- I view him as an hunter who does exactly what he thinks is right. He was abused by a vampire, vampires are the true source of all evil, and if he can extend his lifespan by using the blood of his enemies in order to keep on hunting them down what is bad with that?<br /> <br /> Baudolino uphold the Vigil and does the best to protect the world- and if he turns out messy and bloody it is because the Vigil is messy and bloody.</div> </div> </div> </div>one of my favorite aspects of the Lucifuge and Baudolino is that they are both very flawed, yet truly believe they are doing what is best and true to stay on the path of light. now I do consider Baudolino &quot;cooler&quot; simply because he is able to stale-mate the the much older Lucifuge in conversation and trickery (if 2nd edition still keeps the idea from C&amp;Cs that they also lie and such to each other)<br /> <br /> anyway. yeah, I realize word count is MUCH better spent on the other sections rather than sub factions. it just sorta irks me that some sub factions just seem like &quot;here's if you need them as extremists&quot;<br /> <br /> lastly, damn it, the wrath of Archangel Michael ain't aggravated damage anymore lol.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-17T13:17:07-08:00","id":1368626,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1365834-lostlight-reads-hunter-2e?p=1368536#post1368536\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I still do not see the reason why MM is called this way and they still hunt vampires. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ( Beside 'they boss is previous ghoul' ) Conspiracy is called 'Hammer on Witches', for Popes sake! ( Vampires relation are still not open to this. )</div> </div> </div> </div>Kindred make people immortal by feeding them their blood - the Church in our reality has never been concerned with vampires because it\u2019s never been under the misconception they existed. If they DID, they\u2019d be the highest blasphemy imaginable.<br /> <br /> <br /> ((I up this even further at my own table by making transubstantiated vitae used in Benedictions, borrowing a bit from the Cainite Heresy which I don\u2019t use as such. Besides playing up the theme of taking back the blasphemed blood of Christ, it also covers why Benedictions are a secret the Church doesn\u2019t use for evangelizing purposes))","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 02-17-2020, 04:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-17T17:35:47-08:00","id":1368649,"title":"","content":"even then it makes sense because in real life the catholic church really didn't believe in witchcraft for a long time. in fact it was heresy to say someone was a witch. There was a funny trial were two women confess to using white magic and the inquisitors didn't know what to do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24179-grimmi05","user":"Grimmi05","date":".  Typos 02-17-2020, 10:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24179-grimmi05","name":"Grimmi05","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-17T18:39:04-08:00","id":1368662,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grimmi05</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1365834-lostlight-reads-hunter-2e?p=1368649#post1368649\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">even then it makes sense because in real life the catholic church really didn't believe in witchcraft for a long time. in fact it was heresy to say someone was a witch. There was a funny trail were two women confess to using white magic and the inquisitors didn't know what to do.</div> </div> </div> </div>yeah, as meme worthy as it is, it was mostly secular lawgivers that burned witches (and protestant groups). but this is the chronicles of darkness, where witches very much ARE real. while the MM was more than likely smart enough to know &quot;oh, it's just superstition&quot; they also were savvy to know &quot;that's an ACTUAL witch, he must die if he cant truly repent&quot;<br /> <br /> also <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1098_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1098\" data-vbnamecard=\"1098\">glamourweaver</a>, I do think Vampires very much WOULD be priority number one if the church considered them real. the whole Blood, embrace, and kiss thing is just way too on the nose (in the eyes of Catholics such as myself) to not think &quot;that is a perversion of God and his Bride the Church&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-18T02:22:29-08:00","id":1368702,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1365834-lostlight-reads-hunter-2e?p=1368662#post1368662\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> yeah, as meme worthy as it is, it was mostly secular lawgivers that burned witches (and protestant groups). but this is the chronicles of darkness, where witches very much ARE real. while the MM was more than likely smart enough to know &quot;oh, it's just superstition&quot; they also were savvy to know &quot;that's an ACTUAL witch, he must die if he cant truly repent&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>On the other hand, note that as Sleepers do not remember Awakened magic, and without access to their Endowments those hunters were without doubt Sleepers, it would make sense that most hunters do not actually have had any evidence that witches are real- but as Baudolino showed, vampires were real. Even thaumaturges, IIRC, have some issues in using magic before sleepers, and so if you have a monster which you know is real and one monster you believe is not real, the fact that witches are real doesn't change much in the early MM's history. Only after they become a conspiracy and start understanding the wider world of the CofD they could discover &quot;oh, it looks like witches are a thing after all! Vampires are still worse, of course&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-18T05:56:54-08:00","id":1368722,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1365834-lostlight-reads-hunter-2e?p=1368702#post1368702\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the other hand, note that as Sleepers do not remember Awakened magic, and without access to their Endowments those hunters were without doubt Sleepers, it would make sense that most hunters do not actually have had any evidence that witches are real- but as Baudolino showed, vampires were real. Even thaumaturges, IIRC, have some issues in using magic before sleepers, and so if you have a monster which you know is real and one monster you believe is not real, the fact that witches are real doesn't change much in the early MM's history. Only after they become a conspiracy and start understanding the wider world of the CofD they could discover &amp;quot;oh, it looks like witches are a thing after all! Vampires are still worse, of course&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>you bring up a good point. huh, now that you bring it up, I wonder if 2nd edition will explain Sleepers and Endowments. probably not, but i do find it odd that people who do alchemy, perform miracles from what may be heaven, interact with twilight and such are still affected by quiescence","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-18T07:44:33-08:00","id":1368746,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1365834-lostlight-reads-hunter-2e?p=1368722#post1368722\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> you bring up a good point. huh, now that you bring it up, I wonder if 2nd edition will explain Sleepers and Endowments. probably not, but i do find it odd that people who do alchemy, perform miracles from what may be heaven, interact with twilight and such are still affected by quiescence</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, my personal theory of &quot;Endowments as stabilized Divergence&quot;, that is that the ability to use Endowments requires a certain metaphysical transformation of the hunter in a very subtle way, should be enough for them to be count as Sleepwalkers. While Advanced Armory is a bit contradictory, it should be mentioned that cyborgs are a Deviant Clade, and as such technology can scar the soul enough to turn them into Sleepwalkers, IMO.<br /> <br /> Again, just my personal theory, nothing official.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-18T08:40:41-08:00","id":1368753,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1365834-lostlight-reads-hunter-2e?p=1368746#post1368746\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, my personal theory of &amp;quot;Endowments as stabilized Divergence&amp;quot;, that is that the ability to use Endowments requires a certain metaphysical transformation of the hunter in a very subtle way, should be enough for them to be count as Sleepwalkers. While Advanced Armory is a bit contradictory, it should be mentioned that cyborgs are a Deviant Clade, and as such technology can scar the soul enough to turn them into Sleepwalkers, IMO.<br /> <br /> Again, just my personal theory, nothing official.</div> </div> </div> </div>nothing wrong with that. I forgot what it was called, but you know that Relic the AKD had in Compacts and Conspiracies? the one that let you use relics and gave bonus against mages and werewolves. I also like to think it makes you a Sleepwalker<br /> <br /> I will say actually, the Stabilized Divergence theory is very interesting. it certainly seems to be how Thaumatech works. I shutter to think of what any Divergence from a hunter conspiracy endowment would look like though","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-18T13:01:17-08:00","id":1368788,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1365834-lostlight-reads-hunter-2e?p=1368753#post1368753\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> nothing wrong with that. I forgot what it was called, but you know that Relic the AKD had in Compacts and Conspiracies? the one that let you use relics and gave bonus against mages and werewolves. I also like to think it makes you a Sleepwalker</div> </div> </div> </div>The Oath Stone<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I will say actually, the Stabilized Divergence theory is very interesting. it certainly seems to be how Thaumatech works. I shutter to think of what any Divergence from a hunter conspiracy endowment would look like though </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1023945-hunter-made-deviants\">Yep</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-19T11:23:33-08:00","id":1368977,"title":"","content":"Time to see what the Union and VALKYRIE have prepared for us...<br /> <br /> Regular Schmoes- well, that's one way to put it.<br /> <br /> Evil capitalists are evil capitalists.<br /> <br /> Yeah, there is a reason that you don't just post &quot;hey, I've seen a monster! Let's kill it!&quot; on the internet. Monsters have computers too.<br /> <br /> I start to wonder if perhaps a meld of the Union with some factions of Network 0 could be the key for the later gaining a Conspiracy status...<br /> <br /> Regular schmoes showing monsters who is the boss is basically the core of Hunter's identity.<br /> <br /> I remember that scene in Durarara!! where all of the Dollars worked together to save Anri, or the CROWD of Gatchaman. I think that this is the future of the Union (I wrote a bit about it in Going Up the Tiers)<br /> <br /> Yeah, in the age of the internet and with Netowrk 0's infrastructure, they could indeed become something great- the Vigil in all of its bloody glory. The monsters won't like it, of course, but who asked them?<br /> <br /> I really like the Fire Fighter concept.<br /> <br /> I think that sewage workers are, like, the ones who know the best about the God Machine. Easy to miss, impossible to get rid off, and knowing all of your weak points.<br /> <br /> Ammm I must say that the Politicals rise an interesting point- while in real life we could have a lot of discussion about whether or not gun rights should be limited, in the case of Hunter where you have monsters around every corner limited gun rights could indeed help the monsters more than help the mortals in questions... On the other hand, many slashers also use guns, so we are back to square one.<br /> <br /> I must say that VALKYRIE's art feels a bit underwhelming..I mean, I know that drone fighting is the future, but still.<br /> <br /> I get why it was said &quot;agents in black&quot; instead of &quot;men in black', but it still feels a bit weird. Nothing too important, of course.<br /> <br /> Yep, VALKYRIE is probably a name which shows up in every conspiracy theorists dictionary. I can perfectly imagine the &quot;aliens guy&quot; talking about the super secret agency which was founded by valkyries who were in fact aliens who helped the Nazis during the WWII but switched sides and taught America how to create the atomic bomb. Heck, this is canon now.<br /> <br /> BUT WHAT HAPPENED IN ROSEWELL?!?!<br /> <br /> Was there some data leak in 2013? *short google search* Ah, WikiLeaks. Of course.<br /> <br /> Ooooooooh I like that they actually encourage false conspiracy theories around them in order to hide the truth better.<br /> <br /> *looking at the last paragraph about the conspiracy theories of TFV's agents*<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://imgflip.com/i/3pogsn\" target=\"_blank\">Yeah</a><br /> <br /> It is nice to see that VALKYRIE's agents know that they are manipulated, and do their best to go around it.<br /> <br /> Yeah, what is the big difference between demons and aliens?<br /> <br /> Oh crap, TFV actually recruits civilians who just know too much for their own good? Yikes.<br /> <br /> So between intelligence agents, scientists and cover up squad, who actually in the TFV fights the monsters?<br /> <br /> Yeah, those weapons are 100% tech. There is no issue with bullets than can go through the Twilight or something :P<br /> <br /> Also- yeah, there is nothing weird about advanced technology. It is not like it can BREAK A PERSON'S SOUL or anything. Technology is fine, guys.<br /> <br /> I see they have kept the ammunition concept from the playtest. Nice.<br /> <br /> Yeah, sure the RFID is meant to collect info on agents &quot;in case they get lost&quot;. Not &quot;if they say screw this, I'm having my own conspiracy with blackjack and blood dolls&quot;.<br /> <br /> So they can actually trap a werewolf in a human skin. Man, Luna must be pissed off!<br /> <br /> Yeah, it is nice to see yet another reference for TFV being one of the conspiracies more tended towards forging the &quot;Vigil Alliance&quot;. And of course they are being compromised.. but probably that's not the issue. I mean, why the hell would the vampires who fund TFV's science project kill their own scientists? Something is fishy here. I blame the witches (or, at the very least, the Seers. You should watch what you eat, and Division VI is a poisoned dish).<br /> <br /> And of course, you can;t be a TFV agents without a Mjolnir Cannon!<br /> <br /> Come on, how no TFV agent asked themselves why there are so many Norse mythology references in their conspiracy? It is because they have HYDRA in their organization, that's why.<br /> <br /> I must say I am a bit disappointed that the VDSB does not actually burns vampires like sunlight. I mean, sure, it may be too much to ask from Advanced Armory, but it could have been cool.<br /> <br /> Nice writeups, overall. Now, we have one more and we could get into the bones of the book- splats are fun and all, but I actually want to see what Hunter has to offer beside its amazing organizations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-19T11:55:01-08:00","id":1368985,"title":"","content":"Now I<i> really</i> want to see conflict of SWORN and Union over the same target monster or phenomena. Minorities activists and ecologists vs worker unions. ( And I write it as leftist myself. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1365834-lostlight-reads-hunter-2e?p=1368977#post1368977\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I must say that VALKYRIE's art feels a bit underwhelming..I mean, I know that drone fighting is the future, but still.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's exactly because art shows <i>present</i> - not <i><b>the future</b></i>. VALKYRIE is supposed to have super advanced tech - and on the art we see normal guy with typical drones from nearest tech expo. Common, where is my MJOLNIR cannons?! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-19T12:46:57-08:00","id":1368993,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1365834-lostlight-reads-hunter-2e?p=1368985#post1368985\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now I<i> really</i> want to see conflict of SWORN and Union over the same target monster or phenomena. Minorities activists and ecologists vs worker unions. ( And I write it as leftist myself. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> It's exactly because art shows <i>present</i> - not <i><b>the future</b></i>. VALKYRIE is supposed to have super advanced tech - and on the art we see normal guy with typical drones from nearest tech expo. Common, where is my MJOLNIR cannons?! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I feel like the main issue is that he looks like he is from Network 0, or a Null Mysteriis hunter who utilizes tech to learn about the sociology and behavior of monsters.<br /> <br /> granted it, if the aim was to emphasize how the men in black could be anyone, then it is good work. but it definitely is not what I expected it to be. granted, 1st edition clearly showed the typical SWAT hunter. the man here is the Suit side of TFV","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-19T15:15:22-08:00","id":1369032,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar503_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"503\" data-vbnamecard=\"503\">LostLight</a> just a minor question. how do you feel about the write-up for the General Strike? I was kinda surprised they are still the &quot;get killed a lot&quot; faction we had in the 1st edition core. I was thinking it would be more like a mix of the core and &quot;compacts and conspiracies&quot; supplement write-up. that, and it seems odd that the General Strike is called out as getting killed a ton of times while the Politicals aren't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-19T17:06:58-08:00","id":1369053,"title":"","content":"you would be surprised how many civillians the CIA hires. SOmebody has to do research and who better then people who studied the region and the history of the people living there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24179-grimmi05","name":"Grimmi05","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-19T17:26:54-08:00","id":1369055,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grimmi05</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1365834-lostlight-reads-hunter-2e?p=1369053#post1369053\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">you would be surprised how many civillians the CIA hires. SOmebody has to do research and who better then people who studied the region and the history of the people living there.</div> </div> </div> </div>recruitment for FORT has always interested me. I like to think it's kind of a dumping ground for &quot;crazies&quot;. it does house former cult leaders after all. it serves as both a way to put criminals and occultists to good use while also saying &quot;they don't need too big a budget, weirdoes mostly deal in tomes and rituals anyway&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-21T04:21:36-08:00","id":1369326,"title":"","content":"And for the last Splats preview, we have the brand new Nine Stars and the long loved VASCU!<br /> <br /> Let's start from the Nine Stars-<br /> <br /> The opening quote is a bit bland, but ok<br /> <br /> So are serial killers a big problem in Hong Kong also in real life? Or is there a bit slasher movies culture? The writeup seems very suggestive of it, at the very least.. <br /> <br /> Yep, they are indeed a police based compact, focused around supernatural based crimes (slashers, specifically).<br /> <br /> The fact that slashers are being described as an epidemic makes me wonder if this is something unique to Hong Kong, or if in the CofD, the sudden rise in monsters also means a sudden rise in a number of slashers- or, perhaps, it is mostly a rise in slasher activity. <br /> <br /> Yeah, you shouldn't mix your day job and night job- that's how your life turns into a living hell. <br /> <br /> If the bureaucracy would be what that kills the Nine Stars it would be so ironic.. even though I won;t be surprised if there is a cabal behind it. After all, slashers can grow out of the police just as hunters, and the Hunt Club are known to get friends in high places.<br /> <br /> Ammmm hunger in Hong Kong.. why does it sound so familiar?..<br /> <br /> *enter- the Eater of Names*<br /> <br /> Ah, you. Got it. Go away, please.<br /> <br /> Wait- find new slashers <i>before</i> they strike? Yeah, if regular people just <i>become</i> slashers with no warning in Hong Kong, something must be really wrong in this city. And by really wrong I mean &quot;Stop Eating names You Monster&quot; kind of wrong.<br /> <br /> (yeah, I know it could also be the Contagion, but the Eater of Names of cooler, IMO)<br /> <br /> It is interesting to see how the Nine Stars also have a good potential for interacting with other monsters. I think that if the current incarnation of the Council of Bones would collapse, the Nine Stars could easily replace them. Heck, they could grow independently into their own Chapter, and then unite with the wider conspiracy. That could help them deal with the slasher epidemic.<br /> <br /> I like it that because the Nine Stars are so young, that you can actually play one of the compact's founders.<br /> <br /> So they actually grade you stars for hunting monsters. Kinda cool, saying the truth.<br /> <br /> Amm, I would have preferred to see a VASCU agent art than the opening art of a chapter, but oh well.<br /> <br /> Wait- so VASCU is private/freelancer now? I do like they are more international in scale, however.<br /> <br /> Ahhhh ok, that explains it. Unit rivalry is never good in law enforcement, but is still an integral part of it. Everyone hates it when someone is too successful for their own good.<br /> <br /> So the mysterious Director of Operations was replaced without us ever knowing if the theory of him being a god machine angel was correct (not that there was much to support it in the first place, but the connection between the Room of Mirrors and Beneath the Skin is very suspicious).<br /> <br /> Yeah, so we have replaced the non officially weird Director of Operations with an officially weird mysterious benefactor. Yeah, good for you VASCU.<br /> <br /> Heck, maybe this is Dr. Wintergeen? It would make a lot of sense if she is behind the conspiracy's salvation.<br /> <br /> Yep, Wintergeen.<br /> <br /> You know, it would be extremely ironic if the FBI wants to use VASCU to sniff out Wintergreen, while Wintergeen is the one who bought the conspiracy under a false name.<br /> <br /> And yeah, of course someone wants VASCU dead- people with the ability to unlock minds are not someone people with things to hide wants around.<br /> <br /> And again, I must assume cabals in the government.<br /> <br /> Cooperation with TFV could explain that fiction, where a VASCU agents use terms from VALKYRIE's lexicon.<br /> <br /> I like the Hunters section.<br /> <br /> So even within VASCU the competition never stops.<br /> <br /> So the slasher epidemic is a global thing. in the end?<br /> <br /> I'm a tad disappointed that there wasn't some mechanical support for the Wintergeen Process, to enhance it is dangerous. Sure, the Endowments costing Lethal Damage does enhance it, but still.<br /> <br /> Yeah, the hall of Mirrors is still here and is still fucked up as ever.<br /> <br /> Yeah, melding your mind with that of a cold machine definitely does not scream GOD MACHINE INVOLVEMENT. Nope, not at all.<br /> <br /> Oh, there is no &quot;secret plot hook&quot; sidebar? That's disappointing.<br /> <br /> Anyway, the Nine Stars seems to be very cool, and I think I do like VASCU going private. I do wish to know more about the all &quot;slasher epidemic&quot; thing which is going on, but we'll have to wait for Chapter 7 for this...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-21T04:23:30-08:00","id":1369328,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1365834-lostlight-reads-hunter-2e?p=1369032#post1369032\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar503_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"503\" data-vbnamecard=\"503\">LostLight</a> just a minor question. how do you feel about the write-up for the General Strike? I was kinda surprised they are still the &quot;get killed a lot&quot; faction we had in the 1st edition core. I was thinking it would be more like a mix of the core and &quot;compacts and conspiracies&quot; supplement write-up. that, and it seems odd that the General Strike is called out as getting killed a ton of times while the Politicals aren't.</div> </div> </div> </div>While I generally favor the incorporation of concepts from C&amp;C into 2e, I must admit that I don't have any strong feelings about this specific subject. The General Strike in C&amp;C were cool, but nothing deal breaker.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-21T05:47:58-08:00","id":1369344,"title":"","content":"I like how VASCU is actually in a pretty good place as far as Conspiracies go. They've gotten a new budget, they still have their Endowment, they aren't butting heads with TF:V anymore; really, the main difference is that they have a bigger territory and recruiting pool. They're actually in a better spot than they were originally, shows it isn't all getting worse.<br /> <br /> I'm already fond of Nine Stars too; not hard to imagine them opening up an international chapter either, they're a growing Compact and really, VASCU probably would give them funds. Any help is appreciated, even if it's just guys with shiny medals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-21T11:32:17-08:00","id":1369410,"title":"","content":"the 9 Stars definitely impressed me. I honestly thought they'd be more boring. the fact a founding member is considered recent enough to be playable is cool, and much like habibti ma (or Ma'at, if we want to be correct), I like how this compact is so new as to sorta be &quot;discovering&quot; the monsters in the shadows. I do like the Fellowships too, particularly the five and nine for trying to solve the more overtly supernatural monsters.<br /> <br /> as for VASCU, cant say I'm happy about the private force investigators thing, but I'm not upset about it either. wonder what happened to the Lansing Facility. I actually wonder if they ever get into conflict with the knights of Saint Adrian now","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-24T05:01:24-08:00","id":1370035,"title":"","content":"And after finally finishing the C&amp;C chapter, let's move into the bones of the game-<br /> <br /> Yeah, the Vigil is powered by despair as much as it is powered by hope.<br /> <br /> Same old, same old<br /> <br /> So Touchstone must be something outside of the Vigil- which makes sense. Its point is to anchor you to the normal, day to day life and stop you from falling into zeal and madness. That's how slashers are born, after all.<br /> <br /> Amm- so the concept is that all hunters in a cell must belong to the same tier, which is weird. I am pretty sure that as I understood it, groups like the Lucifuge and Network 0 do work with hunters of lower/ different tiers than they are.<br /> <br /> So Tactics are the defining trait of the cell. Makes sense.<br /> <br /> So Group Beats are the &quot;signature Beats&quot; of Hunter- again, makes sense.<br /> <br /> The &quot;Vigil turn you into a Monster&quot; theme is well reinforced through Touchstones.<br /> <br /> The Confessional Touchstone is a really cool example. The Nosy Neighbor gives a nice example for a negative Touchstone- you hate that gossip, but you must actively care for them so they won't start talking, giving you an hold outside of the Vigil. Even the people you hate can give you something to grasp on when you fight something with eat tentacles and a beak. <br /> <br /> Yeah, not all Integrity 0 people become slashers- but it is much easier to become one when you hit rock bottom.<br /> <br /> So the Vigil is indeed a transmutive process, which shields the psych of the hunter from things a regular person can't handle. The Code solidifies their principles, turning the mind of the hunter into something more resilient to the darkness. The whole description really makes me feel that my view of &quot;hunter as a mortal evolved template&quot; is correct- you are still human, but you have went to the edge of the human soul to gain the power to stand against the darkness, becoming mankind's both best and worst to survive.<br /> <br /> Yeah, becoming an hunter is something you &quot;unlock&quot;- the last stand of the human soul against the night.<br /> <br /> Ok, so I know that after the playtest there were some complaints about how inflexible the Code was in 2e, so let's see how it changed. The idea of &quot;must protect people from monsters&quot; is still a thing, but it does hint that some aspects of the Code are more personalized.<br /> <br /> Yeah, we can clearly see that the writers have read the discussion in the subject- there is a different between the hunter's faith and their instincts. The Code is a representation of the later, not the former. The fact you believe in something doesn't help by much when the Vigil kicks in, but it could help in the form of Touchstones which support you when you violate the Code in the name of you ideals.<br /> <br /> Yeah, the Vigil is not only a virus- it is a parasite. The despair of humanity and its hope for a better future rides you like a meat suit until you burn down.<br /> <br /> Yeah, the Code is represented by what the hunter views- but the fact is that if the hunter knows that what they see is the use of Endowments or Supernatural Merits, the Code does not kick in. That is more ironic as the Lucifuge are in fact monsters, but knowing that they are hunters who use Endowments actually avoids it. It is not ok to use supernatural abilities- but it is ok if it is in the service of the Vigil. I wonder how far can we stretch that definition- I mean, would a warlock who devotes their lives for saving mortals from monsters and claiming to be a part of a cell be described as a person? I mean, while they do use Dread Powers (or their equivalent), what is the difference between them and Endowments if the hunter in question thinks they are Endowments? A monster who fights to save the innocents could, in that context, be described as a person- because they use their powers to fight something much more terrible. That gives a lot of flexibility in the Code, actually.<br /> <br /> Wait- your quarry is another hunter gives you a +2? Well, if you wondered if hunters are monsters...<br /> <br /> Helping a monster is still a negative modifier, but is not a breaking point by itself.<br /> <br /> So an Exceptional Success in a Breaking Point has its own faults.<br /> <br /> So yeah, a sidebar referring to the whole discussion- the Code is not meant to force you to act in a certain way. It means to make you pay for your choices. Just like how vampires can try and be as human as possible, hunters can be devoted to the Code as much as possible- but there is a price to pay, and violating the Code has a price on its own.<br /> <br /> And here we emphasis again the difference between tiers in game- it is really a shame that each organization doesn't come with their own description of a Creed, and how its interacts with the Code. It could have been really helpful, IMO.<br /> <br /> I also would have preferred if it wasn't a &quot;one time deal&quot;.<br /> <br /> Yeah, yeah, nobody cares about attributes and skills here :P<br /> <br /> Merits are merits. I like the seance Devotee.<br /> <br /> So two things- first, isn't it the first time that it is stated that zero Integrity removes your ability to use Supernatural Merits? Second, nice note that the Lucifuge are human enough to use those Merits.<br /> <br /> Aaand that's it for now! I need to go to the gym. I'll review the rest either later today or tomorrow.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-24T10:27:30-08:00","id":1370085,"title":"","content":"Ok, time to move to the next preview-<br /> <br /> *skipping general rules*<br /> <br /> Risking Willpower- the core Hunter feature :P<br /> <br /> So Risking Willpower is the purest form of despair- it always comes out of a place of weakness, when all hell breaks loose (literally) and the hunter is willing to sacrifice themselves in the name of the Vigil. If you are not on the edge, you can't reach into the depths of your soul to find that power reserve. I personally would have preferred if an hunter could also risk Willpower in other times of crises, but oh well.<br /> <br /> *skipping general rules*<br /> <br /> Teamwork and Tactics!<br /> <br /> So yeah, Teamwork is pretty standard.<br /> <br /> I must admit I really liked how the last fiction described hunters using a Tactic. It was really cool.<br /> <br /> So Tactics relay on the same source of power as Risking Willpower and the Code- drawing oneself into the edge, and gaining hope out of despair. Those chapters really emphasis that the existence of an hunter comes from being pushed into the corner, both mentally, physically and spiritually. I still can see other events that could push people to the edge to touch the same source of inner power, but I guess that pushing your mind daily against monsters is the best way to reach that state. <br /> <br /> The mechanics for Tactics look interesting. I think they really feel like how a Tactic should feel.<br /> <br /> Bind/Ward is, like, really cool.<br /> <br /> Yeah, Identification goes well with my thoughts about how hunters may mistake a normal person into a monster, and then hunt them as such.<br /> <br /> Yeah, Harvest is specially made for Cheiron hunters.. as well as Null Mysteriis.<br /> <br /> Freeing Mind is probably something used by the Habibti Maa.<br /> <br /> Overall, I think I really like how Tactics are being constructed in this edition. Not that different from 1e, IIRC, but still good.<br /> <br /> I must say I am a tad disappointed that hunters didn't got anything extra. I mean, Tactics, Risking Willpower and the Code were the same features of being an hunter in 1e, and the pre-Kickstarter description made me think that perhaps they are going to get some extra things to define themselves. Sure, those three are great, but I kinda hoped for something new?<br /> <br /> Anyway, Appendix review (which should be short, I think)<br /> <br /> Equipment is equipment.<br /> <br /> Wow, that's a lot of ways to skin a hellcat. Costume gear is cool.<br /> <br /> But your leg! Ah! It's caught in a bear trap!<br /> <br /> (ironically, the first example trap is a bear trap. Oh, Shia, Shia, Shia..)<br /> <br /> Tilts are tilts.<br /> <br /> Conditions are conditions.<br /> <br /> I must say that I miss those days where one of the appendices have actually detailed a supporting splat in details. Sure, last time we had those was in Geist, and Mummy stuffed it all into antagonists and such, and Hunter doesn't really have a support minor splat other than regular people, but still, I think it gave some deeper ground to the game.. oh well.<br /> <br /> Anyway, that's it! Next preview- Monsters, on the 26th! Stay tuned :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-24T12:27:20-08:00","id":1370117,"title":"","content":"Actually, according to Monica, there is one more system, it's just part of the Slasher Chronicle.<br /> <br /> Namely, risking turning into a slasher. That's going to be interesting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-25T19:53:35-08:00","id":1370491,"title":"","content":"Did I missed Bygones or they weren't shared in last previous package?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-26T03:50:01-08:00","id":1370525,"title":"","content":"I'm wondering if I somehow missed the Endowment creation rules but they might be in the Storytelling chapter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-26T04:51:05-08:00","id":1370531,"title":"","content":"And for the next preview- Who Run The World? Mons(ters)!<br /> <br /> (sorry... not sorry)<br /> <br /> Nice opening paragraph.<br /> <br /> Amm interesting- Monica did mentioned once that instead of providing a sample settings they are taking a different path for world building, and I assume that the monsters presented in here is one such paths.<br /> <br /> The fun thing is that usually, when another gameline incorporate a monster from an urban legend, they usually take the path of &quot;the monster's version in literature is not correct, here is how it actually works&quot;. In Hunter, it seems that the monsters would be much closer to their mythical origin- even though that's also how things work for regular mortals, so..<br /> <br /> So yeah, horrors are horrors.<br /> <br /> Ah, yes, the evil tooth faerie is a thing.<br /> <br /> Damnation is EVIL<br /> <br /> I love the Beshilu reference.<br /> <br /> I'm a bit surprised that Glitch referred to a warlock instead of a demon.<br /> <br /> Oh- here is the Infernal Dread Power.<br /> <br /> So yeah, the Infernal Dread Power more or less marks a monster as something from hell.<br /> <br /> <i>Song of My Soul, My Voice is Dead,<br /> Die Thou, Unsung, as Tears Unshed,<br /> Shall Dry and Die in<br /> Lost Carcosa</i><br /> <br /> (yeah, if Madness and Terror is NOT a King in Yellow reference, I don't know what it is)<br /> <br /> She gets down on all fours and breaks into a sprint!<br /> <br /> Yeah, being immortal is a Dread Power.<br /> <br /> It's not a witch that throws lightning at you, it's God- not straighten up, young man!<br /> <br /> I must admit that it is a bit strange that Hunter doe snot includes Angels in the Ephemeral Entities section, as the Core does- but on the other hand, the Core also includes the God Machine Chronicles, so it makes sense.<br /> <br /> Ephemera is ephemera.<br /> <br /> Monsters by Region!<br /> <br /> So Padfoot is an actual nickname for Black Dogs- I learned something new!<br /> <br /> I do like Black Dogs.<br /> <br /> Goddammit they said that slenderman was a lie! I was lied to! Liars! All liars!<br /> <br /> Why the &quot;Wheel of Fire&quot; as a relic sounds familiar?...<br /> <br /> Mongolian Death Worm- cause why not?<br /> <br /> Hungry Grass is just plain old weird, in a good way.<br /> <br /> Yeah, I think that those Ants are the ones from Witch Finders (and I am pretty sure either they or the locust had a cameo in Deviant). I do wish the game would have developed more of those plot hooks from the history section of 1e.<br /> <br /> Sea Trow- yikes!<br /> <br /> Subterranean Humanoids because why not?<br /> <br /> Didn't we already got the Teke Teke in Hurt Locker?<br /> <br /> And those are the monsters! Next time, the places they call home!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":503,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","user":"LostLight","date":". 02-26-2020, 08:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-26T06:13:50-08:00","id":1370541,"title":"","content":"Yeah, the moment Slender Man showed up, I immediately decided that Network Zero has him filed under N in the alphabetical files (for &quot;NOPE NOPE NOPE NOPE&quot;).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-26T09:59:42-08:00","id":1370588,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1365834-lostlight-reads-hunter-2e?p=1370491#post1370491\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Did I missed Bygones or they weren't shared in last previous package?</div> </div> </div> </div>That Bygone section is in the Mysterious Places chapter.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1870-mlvalentine","name":"mlvalentine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1870_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-26T10:00:23-08:00","id":1370589,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1365834-lostlight-reads-hunter-2e?p=1370525#post1370525\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm wondering if I somehow missed the Endowment creation rules but they might be in the Storytelling chapter.</div> </div> </div> </div>Endowment creation rules are in the Storyteller's chapter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1870-mlvalentine","name":"mlvalentine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1870_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-26T10:31:21-08:00","id":1370595,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1365834-lostlight-reads-hunter-2e?p=1370541#post1370541\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, the moment Slender Man showed up, I immediately decided that Network Zero has him filed under N in the alphabetical files (for &quot;NOPE NOPE NOPE NOPE&quot;).</div> </div> </div> </div>Ironically, it is Network Zero's writeup which said that the crrepy guy in a suit is fake- and then, we get it in the monsters section!* I feel so betrayed! And that's after I had a slenderman nightmare a few nights ago :P<br /> <br /> *legal issues aside, of course. I assume that it won't be that much of a difficulty to resking the slenderman into something more generic with the same concept, but that depends on how things would roll.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-28T05:56:40-08:00","id":1370994,"title":"","content":"And here is our next preview- Mysterious Places!<br /> <br /> I must say that I am pretty excited towards this section- the blog post alone has inspired me to immediately write the<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1224144-domus-sanctus-compact\"> Domus Sanctus</a> as a compact that had to deal with tainted, hungry places. Monica has also asked us to give some extra attention to those chapters, for the represent new additions to Hunter, and as such I am going to do my best and give a deep look at those strange, mysterious places.<br /> <br /> So- let's start reading, shall we?<br /> <br /> Yeah, many times the true horror is not the monster itself as the place it lurks in. I mean, in the original Paranormal Activity movie, the demon is an unseen threat- it is the house which creeps you out. The best kind of horror, IMO, is the one in which you don't see the monster- you only see the place it calls home, and as such, the lair and the monster becomes one- the lair serves as the &quot;face&quot; of evil. The world is tainted, and there is nothing you can do about it other than burning it with fire.<br /> <br /> Yeah, so Nests are the standard &quot;monster lairs&quot;, Tainted place are where evil seeps into the ground and bad things just happen, and Sentient places are when the place itself is the monster. Among the tree, I think that Tainted are the most terrifying- those are places where the world is just wrong, points in the world where the natural fabric collapse upon itself, and the darkness fills the holes. There is no secret agenda, not monster you can banish, no meaning in the bad things which happen there. People die and suffer and break and turn into monsters by themselves not because the place wants to ruin their lives, but because that's just how those places work. THAT is the natural order. This world is fucked up, and you are just another causality in the natural darkness of the world. It is like the difference between fearing a pack of hungry wolves and fearing a natural cataclysm. The first will eat you, but you can fight against it, or at least develop tools to protect yourself from it- but when the very world turns against you, when the earth crumbles beneath your feet and the sky spit lightning and hail, there isn't much you can do but covering your head and pray.<br /> <br /> Yeah, Bygones sounds really creepy. Like, evil places in miniature.<br /> <br /> I wonder how the AKD deals with Bygones.<br /> <br /> The concept of sentient places making Bygones reminds me of that Wheel of Time damned city which produced a dagger which carried its evil beyond its borders.<br /> <br /> So semi permanent Bygones are those items which grant a benefit in one hand, and curse with the other. Sounds like Mummy's vessels, IMO.<br /> <br /> So the AKD deals probably with True Bygones, I assume.<br /> <br /> Yeah, it seems that True Bygones actually grant Endowments to their users. I wonder what it means for conspiracies.<br /> <br /> Ok, so let's sum this section up- we have temporary Bygones, which are usually temporary creations which force a Condition when used. Then we have semi permanent Bygones, which are somewhat sentient and give both a benefit and a curse in the form of a Condition or Tilt. Finally, we have true Bygones, which are outright legendary artifacts which grant Endowments to their users, but also hold great danger. In D&amp;D terms, temporary Bygones are potions, scrolls and charged items, semi permanent are the common wondrous items and true are the outright artifacts and leftovers of the gods.<br /> <br /> Yeah, mysterious places and/or Bygones make a great Chronicle for a Tier 1 hunters.<br /> <br /> I now wonder how horrible the Nest of a slasher would be.., Jeepers creepers- like, literally.<br /> <br /> The transition from a mysterious place as an outright threat to a potential resource feels like a nice way to show the difference in attitude between Tier 1 and 2.<br /> <br /> The Long Night would be something really fun to play in a cursed church or something.<br /> <br /> Yeah, all of the Blair Witch/ Paranormal Activity kind of films are standard Network Zero studying mysterious places scenarios.<br /> <br /> NO! BAD NULL MYSTERIIS! STOP FEEDING THE HOUSE JUST TO SEE HOW MUCH BLOOD THE WALLS CAN CRY!<br /> <br /> I still feel that the Union are, like the worst nightmare that monsters have. The last thing you want as a monster is to discover that the whole neighborhood is against you, and that they will come at you with everything they have.<br /> <br /> And here we go Global.<br /> <br /> Yeah, here we go full &quot;mysterious places and Bygones are objects to acquire, researched and be used, not threats to fight against&quot;. At least, not necessarily.<br /> <br /> So the Ascending Ones seem to cover the &quot;relic collector&quot; niche of the core groups. Now I wonder how it is going to work with the AKD's presentation in the &quot;how to make a conspiracy&quot; guidelines...<br /> <br /> Having Cheiron putting a Bygone inside of you sounds TERRIFYING. Also, the way that they turn into occult real estate is very bad news- especially considering C&amp;C. You remember what the Director Boards' next project was, right? Colonization. <br /> <br /> I must say that the interest that the Council has in mysterious places and Bygones does give them some more character, IMO.<br /> <br /> Yeah, Lucifuge, that's called Malleus Loci.<br /> <br /> I can perfectly see a secret order of the MM which deals with cursed places and objects, while stocking the remains of dead saints in the Vatican.<br /> <br /> Asking &quot;how far would the AKD go to get a Bygone&quot; is like asking &quot;how far would an apple fall when dropped&quot;. The answer is &quot;as much as possible, until they'll crush into the ground&quot;.<br /> <br /> And here we are starting with Nests, which monsters lurk.<br /> <br /> I do like how Nests are presented.<br /> <br /> You know what could be FUN? Having a monster making a number of false Nests to mess with hunters which may come for it :P<br /> <br /> Oh, so that's how they add the example settings. Nice.<br /> <br /> I always liked Ship Graveyards.<br /> <br /> Garmelie: &quot;NO THEATER!&quot;<br /> <br /> Yeah, the King in Yellow is now canon :P<br /> <br /> Yeah, a lab dedicated for researching snakes in the CofD- what can go wrong?<br /> <br /> TAINTED<br /> <br /> Yeah, creepy as hell.<br /> <br /> So tainted places ARE monsters- just not monsters that can think or work actively. The very world is a monster, and it is hungry.<br /> <br /> I do like the triggering system for tainted places.<br /> <br /> 13 as a bad sign in a classic.<br /> <br /> Death amusement park is also a classic.<br /> <br /> Yeah, the Lucifuge and/or the Otodo must do something with the Villa.<br /> <br /> I'm surprised that Infernal is not in the list of Dread Powers for a gate to Hell.<br /> <br /> I wonder how the Oak goes with Chris Allen's concept of envious and angry oak trees.<br /> <br /> And now, not only that the world is broken, it also hates you- sentients!<br /> <br /> So 1408? (at least, the movie version)<br /> <br /> So tainted places may be stillborn sentient places, or the corpses of sentient ones.<br /> <br /> Yeah, I won't be surprised if Nautilus is a false identity Cheiron use to get their hand over mysterious places.<br /> <br /> So sentient places are outright spiritual beings. I would have preferred them to used the standard rules for monsters.<br /> <br /> Wait- that statue is an actual thing?! That's just disgusting... I wonder if its heart is a Bygone.<br /> <br /> Yeah, you should never make a fort fall in love with you.<br /> <br /> Yeah, that's what we need- another failed Atlantis. Like Irem wasn't enough.<br /> <br /> I must say I'm surprised that an whole ancient city which serves as a relic of a mythic past is not of Rank 4, at the very least.<br /> <br /> The Grotto is veeeery creepy.<br /> <br /> I am pretty sure that the Aokigahara Forest was already described in one of Demon's supplements- but yeah, it had to show up in here.<br /> <br /> Mulanje as an ecosystem of horrors sounds like a great plot hook.<br /> <br /> Cursed gold and ghosts trains- do we need something more?<br /> <br /> House on the Rock? That's where the gods gather!<br /> <br /> Yeah, cursed highways are evil.<br /> <br /> And that's it! I must say that I hoped that the chapter would be longer, and I am very disappointed that it did not provided any example Bygones together with the mysterious places, but whatever was presented in the book was really good, IMO. I still think that sentient places would have been cooler if they were described as Horrors instead of Ephemerals, but i can see the rational.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-29T00:33:56-08:00","id":1371203,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1365834-lostlight-reads-hunter-2e?p=1370994#post1370994\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So tainted places ARE monsters- just not monsters that can think or work actively. The very world is a monster, and it is hungry.</div> </div> </div> </div>This makes me very reminiscent of <b>Geist</b> 2E Underworld as 'hungry system' - maybe some relation to the whole universe of Chronicles of Darkness?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-02T14:43:38-08:00","id":1372334,"title":"","content":"Ok, so it was a long day with some ups and downs, but finally I have a time to read the new preview- so let's go through it!<br /> <br /> Also, as this preview should give us the tools to design compacts and conspiracies, I am going to use those rules (probably tomorrow) in order to update a single organization from 1e to 2e, just to test my ability to utilize those rules into practice. I'm currently thinking about either the Promethean Brotherhood, Les Mysteres or the Hototogisu, but still haven't decided. (I actually wanted to do the update while reading, but it is too late already so whatever)<br /> <br /> Anyway, here we go!<br /> <br /> Nice opening quote.<br /> <br /> I love the opening paragraph.<br /> <br /> I like that the chapter takes the wordcount to describe that in Hunter, you walk a fine line between having your players too bored or annoyed by either the feeling that things repeat themselves, or that there is no hope for victory. You may be the underdog, but the Vigil should still be exciting and interesting, getting you motivated to practice the hunt yet not feel too confident about your victories.<br /> <br /> A section about how exactly the definition of &quot;monster&quot; in the Code should be utilized. Good.<br /> <br /> I like the different ways that the Code can be interpreted between groups.<br /> <br /> I do like the conflict between hunters and society. It reinforce the tension in which hunters constantly live, and how slashers could be born from it.<br /> <br /> Oh, I do like the conflict between hunters and cults. The concept of such conflict was already presented in 1e, and it is a dark mirror for the hunter's existence. The way that monsters could grant Dread Powers reinforce how cultists are different from hunters, and that sometimes, humans can become monsters due to their devotion for the strange and unearthly.<br /> <br /> The Sodality is a very cool concept for a cult, IMO.<br /> <br /> The fact that even cults without a monstrous patron could develop unnatural Dread Powers further emphasis how fucked up in the CofD's setting. Nice.<br /> <br /> Hunter vs Hunter- because, of course.<br /> <br /> Funny how the most basic kind of conflict- hunters and monsters- is kept to the last.<br /> <br /> That section does give a lot of cool twists made to make the hunt less trivial and more personal and disturbing. It is one thing to hunt an unholy abomination. It is another when discovering it is still a terrified child on the inside who just want help with what it became.<br /> <br /> Knowledge is power, indeed.<br /> <br /> Yeah, the moment that hunters discover that they are not fighting a vampire but a whole fucking covenant of bloodsuckers which have bloodbound the police and mayor is the moment they start screaming.<br /> <br /> Yeah, the Code constantly pushes towards alienation from society, while ironically some monsters have better ties in it.<br /> <br /> Goddammit Mister White- you are still here?!<br /> <br /> I like it that White is almost a sympathetic character, which shows you that even demons can confuse hunters- especially if they have a common enemy.<br /> <br /> The section about losing is very important.<br /> <br /> I like how the chapter presents Tier 1 hunters.<br /> <br /> Clubs, Gangs and Rivalries- an excellent way to describe compacts :P<br /> <br /> I do like the Long Night as the &quot;bringers of hope&quot;, and the suggestion that you could easily have the same concept for other religious groups (well, perhaps less apocalyptic, but still).<br /> <br /> I do like the way it presented the Loyalists as the power which binds other hunters together through knowledge and research.<br /> <br /> So the greatest power of Network Zero is also their weakness- too much information.<br /> <br /> COMPACT CREATION RULES<br /> <br /> Yes, concept is indeed important. The Abbey's is indeed a solid one.<br /> <br /> Foundation is an interesting way to look at it.<br /> <br /> History is indeed important- especially if it is sometimes false. No special changes for the Abbey here.<br /> <br /> So yeah, Faction is the general name in case the organization doesn't have a special one for them. The way cliques are presented, even if short, still manages to bring fourth the different faces of the Abbey. Good work.<br /> <br /> Weird that the rules about Status benefit didn't said what they see as &quot;balanced&quot; for such benefits.<br /> <br /> Conspiracy Theories indeed.<br /> <br /> Yeah, conspiracies do change through time- just ask Cheiron, or however they currently call themselves.<br /> <br /> I do enjoy that conspiracies are so busy at seeing themselves as the top that hunters can reach, that they fail to see how little do they know about the darkness. Oh, don't feel bad- the monsters are just as clueless as you are.<br /> <br /> I do like how varied the Ascending Ones are presented.<br /> <br /> Yeah, Cheiron are the most vicious group in the core- the idea they may even hunt for other hunters is terrifying, and emphasis how the view of the Code could influence hunters.<br /> <br /> I must say that the short passage of the Council does give them more character, IMO- it recognize that they are arrogant and hypocrite, stuck in the past and don't really know with who or what they are dealing. It is a nice touch.<br /> <br /> Why the Lucifuge are &quot;unlikely&quot; to redeem a rogue organization?<br /> <br /> I do like how VALKYRIE may encourage other governments to produce their own groups sponsored by VALKYRIE. I would have suggested one for Israel, for example, but I already have my own canon for how Israel's Vigil work, of course.<br /> <br /> CREATING A CONSPIRACY<br /> <br /> I do like how the concept for a conspiracy is different from a compact, scale wise.<br /> <br /> Oh, i like the concept for the Hook- it helps to ground conspiracies and give them goals, and that while conspiracies are more committed to the Vigil they also give a much greater freedom for their members in terms of worldview.<br /> <br /> So the AKD still hunt for relics. I wonder how their relics differ from Bygones, and if they are not what would make them special on that respect.<br /> <br /> Ohhhhh I really liked that they maintained the whole Paradise Lost theme of the AKD- the search for the relics of fallen lands in hopes for restoring their fallen glory, their grudge against those who exiled them and anger towards those who ruined Paradise before they had a chance to return is very powerful and evocative, and could easily be tied to Mummy as it is tied to Mage and Werewolf.<br /> <br /> Yeah, recruitment is an important tool for conspiracies.<br /> <br /> ENDOWMENT DESIGN<br /> <br /> Yeah, the design itself seems very like the preview- even though it allows a large flexibility, as seen in practice. Cool.<br /> <br /> Ah, finally, relics<br /> <br /> So yeah, relics are Bygones.<br /> <br /> While I did liked to read the suggestions for how the AKD may limit access to their relics, I would have prefered if they were to choose which one they see as the best for them. Usually, gaining Endowments is a transmutation process, and how to implement it to the AKD feels kinda important. The requirement to know keywords is cool.<br /> <br /> I do like the detailed way that Relics design was described, but I really would have wanted more of those! :P Well, maybe if we'll get the third expansion, we would see a more detailed version of the AKD.<br /> <br /> Anyway, that's it for the review. Tomorrow I am going to try the design by myself, and see how it goes!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-03T16:00:10-08:00","id":1372562,"title":"","content":"So, let's start the experiment, shall we?<br /> <br /> Because the book presents the compact creation rules as somewhat different from the conspiracy creation ones, I'm going to do a little update for both tiers- the first would be, of course, the compact, which was chosen to be the <b>Keepers of the Source</b>. The reason? I like those bastards. Yeah yeah, I know, Mage says that they are wrong. i say that Mage is wrong and should mind its own business. Now after clearing this part of the discussion, let's see what we have here-<br /> <br /> <b>Concept:</b> the Keepers of the Source are hunters which are motivated by their love for Mother Earth, and which seeks to protect sacred places from being used by monsters.<br /> <br /> <b>Foundation:</b> the Keepers of the Source use their dowsing sense in order to track down the places they swear to protect, as well as notice when a monster is abusing it.<br /> <br /> <b>History:</b> the compact was founded in the 70s in San Francisco, by a woman who called herself Sunflower. Blessed with a psychic ability called &quot;dowsing&quot; which allowed her to track down ley lines, she gathered a group of faithful to celebrate the powers of Mother Earth. One of those faithful, however, was an actual witch, which used Sunflower's maps in order draw upon the magical Source. The act was felt as a mental backlash for Sunflower, who then tried to convince the witch to return the magic she have taken- yet the witch ignored her pleads. While another member who was also blessed with the dowsing sense, Redgrove, wanted to react with violence, Sunflower objected, leading the new Dowsing Society into a diplomatic effort to explain witches and monsters that Mother Earth should be protected, not used.<br /> <br /> Things changed in 1975, when the Society came into conflict with a pack of werewolves over a sacred sight. With twelve members dead and Sunflower maimed, Redgrove took over the group, leading it into a more violent way of action using ambushes and terrorism. Eventually, at 1985, Redgrove changed the compact's name into the Keepers of the Source, and led it until 1996, when he was killed by a strange lightning strike. Since the 9/11, the Keepers' tactics became more subtle, working as a part of protest groups meant to protect Mother Earth from both mundane and supernatural threats.<br /> <br /> <b>Factions:</b> the Keepers of the Source follow three main philosophies. The <b>Children of Gaia</b> are the followers of Sunflower's original ideals of pacifism and education, believing that monsters must be taught about the consequences of their actions instead of engaging unnecessary conflicts. The <b>Hand of the Mother</b>, however, favor Redgrove's more direct and active approach, as Mother Earth is in dire need and there is no time for monsters correcting their ways, and that they deserve no mercy for defiling the sacred places. Finally, the <b>Dynasts</b> follow Redgrove's daughter, Karen- she believes that the compact is meant to leave legacy after it, and that while outright pacifism would achieve nothing, extreme violence is also not the solution, and instead the Keepers should find the middle ground, and create a better future together.<br /> <br /> <b>Status:</b> Among the Keepers, Status is earned by both protecting Mother Earth from being defiled as well as by finding new discoveries about the dowsing sense and the nature and location of ley lines and Sources.<br /> <br /> 0- You have taken part in protests and dealt mostly in the mundane side of protecting Mother Earth, and as such showed you worthy for the other side of the compact. You are taught some new tools meant to help you in your Vigil for the Mother. You gain one of the following specialties, of your choice- Weaponry (Improved Weapons), Expression (Protests) or Science (Environmentalism)<br /> <br /> 000- You have fought against both supernatural and mundane threats to Earth, showing your worth to your allies and friends. You gain two free dots in Allies (Keepers of the Source) for free.<br /> <br /> 00000- You have been accepted into the inner circles of the Dowser Society and were gifted with one of their greatest abilities- the dowsing sense. You gain the Unseen Senses (Source) merit for free.<br /> <br /> So yeah, compacts are pretty easy to convert- I've had some thoughts about giving the compact Gut Feeling instead, but I think that considering the more psychic nature of dowsing it is better represented as Unseen Senses. It could also be that only a selected few develop dowsing (which is an Unseen Sense) while the most simply learn to notice the ebbs in ley lines through investigation (as Guts Feeling), but both can work.<br /> <br /> Now for some real challenge.. we are going to update a conspiracy. That is, <b>Les Mysteres</b>.<br /> <br /> <b>Concept:</b> we wish to create an organization of shamans and spiritualists which try to bridge between spirit and flesh.<br /> <br /> <b>Hook:</b> we want to maintain a many faced and syncretic structure for Les Mysteres, where individual cells develop their own tools and views for how to commune with the spirit world through their own religious lenses, all united by their will to maintain harmony between worlds.<br /> <br /> <b>History:</b> shamans, mediums and spirit whisperers have always been around, standing on the edges of society as they serve as a bridge between the mundane and the mysteries. Deemed as witches and heretics by some, those shamans worked to serve as a channel between humanity and their gods, delivering the words of the beyond while pleading on the behalf of the people with the divine. While many of those shamans walked alone, during the time of the Oyo Empire those disparate people formed an alliance together, forming a small conspiracy which guided the people of West Africa to the whispers of the Orisha, the sea and sky. Yet, as the Oyo Empire declined and fell into civil war, the conspiracy has shattered- and with the coming of the British colonialists and the transatlantic slave trade, those shattered remains sailed across the sea, until they reached the New World.<br /> <br /> Forced to convert into Christianity, the shamans turned slaves have learned to give new names to the old gods. After all, whether in Africa or in the Americas, be them saints or orisha, the spirits were still there, and the people still needed someone to talk with them on their behalf. In an attempt to combine aspects of Christianity, the many West African faiths and local American religions, new religions were born, and old rituals were incorporated into new structures to fit the cacophony of traditions and practices. And as Haiti claimed independence and revolted against the French rule, those who know the Mysteries, Les Mysteres, were there to call upon the gods and guide the once slaves towards freedom.<br /> <br /> Through their spirit allies, Les Mysteres has started to contact other remains of the old African religion in the New Worlds, as well as followers of other religions. Each land had its own spirits, and as such it was required to learn how to incorporate the local traditions in order to maintain the balance between the worlds. Native American shamanism, Pentecostals and many other priests and spirit talkers found a place among Les Mysteres as the young conspiracy grew across the world. With the Great awakenings of spiritualism, new and innovative practices were added to the Mysteries, eventually even adding things like aliens and advanced thought-forms into the list of faces the conspiracy used in order to commune with their gods.<br /> <br /> However, that variety was also the doom of the conspiracy. While syncretism was the catalyst for Les Mysteres to form, between the constant manipulations of the spirits, the general lack of trust by other hunters for their witch like practices and the constant attacks by werewolves and shapeshifters which claimed them to violate the boundary between the worlds, the alliance between different cells was simply not enough, and the organization have slowly broke apart. Some local cells and compacts still claim heritage from the original conspiracy, but many have just returned to their old ways of taking care of their local community. While the conspiracy is considered to be defunct, the embers are still burning beneath the surface. In the Caribbean and South America, the spirit emissaries still name themselves a Les Mysteres, and they constantly work in order to rebuild what was lost. They grew too fast and collapsed because of it- and a more syncretic attitude must be taken if the conspiracy wishes to rise from the ashes. Thousand voices who sing together may be loud, yet without a single vision the spirits would steal their voices to make them their own and a cacophony would swallow the world. The Vigil must be lite again, leading the way for the Mysteries to sing a new song for the spirits.<br /> <br /> <b>Recruitment:</b> Once Les Mysteres offered its protection and membership to anyone who knew how to speak with the spirits. However, after the fall of the conspiracy, they became far more selective with their members, choosing only those which are willing to combine their world views together. While many of the conspiracy's members belong to afro-american religions, they do not forbid shamans of other religions from joining them, as long as they are willing to accept that the core belief that the truth has many faces, and that no single spiritual tradition knows it all.<br /> <br /> <b>Factions:</b> Les Mysteres is still rebuilding from the wrecks, but some of its old factions has managed to survive together.<br /> <br /> The <b>Children of the Loa</b> are the collectors of ancient traditions and spiritual literature, working actively to rebuild whatever was lost to the conspiracy by studying from thousands of cultures.<br /> <br /> The <b>Society of the Vineyard</b> works to bind the Mysteres to the community around them, working both to serve their local people and spirits and to cultivate connections with other hunters in an attempt to forge trust and alliances.<br /> <br /> The <b>Watchers in the Crossroads </b>seek to unite the many shamans through their devotion to fight werewolves and others who may prey upon the emissaries for their attempts to bridge between flesh and spirit.<br /> <br /> <b>Status:</b> Les Mysteres recognize those who work to maintain balance between the worlds, as well as those who work towards unity through diversity and the rediscovery of new or lost spiritual techniques. Balance, creativity and new innovations are what the Mysteres seek for in order to rise from their ruins.<br /> <br /> 0- You have talked with the spirits and decided to serve as an emissary to the Shadow. You gain Occult (spiritualism) specialty for free.<br /> <br /> 000- You have fought spiritual abominations while protecting sacred sites, and served both your community and your gods, and have learned how to resist the whispers of the Beyond to maintain your will. You may treat your Resolve as higher by one when resisting effects related to spiritual possession or other attempts to control your mind.<br /> <br /> 00000- You have rose to become a new promise for the future of the conspiracy, and a potential leader to guide it. The other hunters gather around you as a spiritual teacher, giving you the equivalent of a four dots Retainer.<br /> <br /> <br /> Well, I wanted to also start and convert some Endowments for Les Mysteres- but it is already late in here and I have work tomorrow, so I'll do it after reading the last chapter of the manuscript- the Slasher Chronicles! As such, a Rites du Cheval conversion would be presented either tomorrow or on Thursday. Hope you'll like it!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-03T17:45:13-08:00","id":1372583,"title":"","content":"Ahh, the Keepers of the Source are very underappreciated compact. Is it ok if I ask some questions about how you see their perspective about the sites they protect, and some specifics regarding the sub factions?<br /> <br /> Also, while I think your Les mysteres write-up is a good way to show them as a &quot;re-building&quot; conspiracy, I admittedly prefer them back as as more disparate with the unique factions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-04T06:04:56-08:00","id":1372692,"title":"","content":"And now that we have conspiracies, let's see how things are going for the Slasher Chronicles- the BBEGs of Hunter.<br /> <br /> So a &quot;caution&quot; note in the opening of the chapter?<br /> <br /> Again, I must say that while I can get behind &quot;monsters are up at higher numbers&quot;, serial killers is a bit weird for me- where I live, thankfully, such instances are really rare, so it is hard for me, from world building perspective, to think how to connect to it. Also, and it is a big also, it seems that the book have not mentioned any theories for WHY we have such a dramatic increase in monsters in general- no theories or possible hooks or something. It feels like the book is building towards something, but towards what?<br /> <br /> Well, it seems I spoke too soon- at least slashers have a number of theories about them.<br /> <br /> There is no reason is simple way to solve it.<br /> <br /> Mass hysteria could make sense in the CofD.<br /> <br /> Humanity is sick serves well a Contagion Chronicles crossover.<br /> <br /> Hunters become slashers- like duh? :P<br /> <br /> Monsters are using slashers is not exactly my cup of tea.<br /> <br /> Hunters creating slashers? Well, that's just hubris.<br /> <br /> Yeah, so Slasher to a mortal is like, a Draugr to a vampire, or Rapt to a mage. The very soul and psych of the person is broken, leaving only madness behind. So yeah, &quot;hunter&quot; is the &quot;evolved mortal template&quot; and slasher is the &quot;fallen mortal template&quot;, IMO.<br /> <br /> Yeah, losing Touchstones seems to be a part of how hunters fall into slasherhood.<br /> <br /> So yeah, slashers could be a product of a long eradication of identity and integrity, the result of some supernatural power breaking one's soul, or even &quot;just&quot; a spontaneous process where a perfectly normal human beings goes through the wrong experience in the wrong place and the wrong time and just snaps. I wonder that it didn't suggested if some slashers are simply born this way- murder children are a trope in the genre, after all.<br /> <br /> Undertakings are still around.<br /> <br /> So yeah, if rippers are mortals, the Code actually says you should protect them over monsters. Fun, ah?<br /> <br /> So yeah, rippers and scourges are still tied by their Undertakings.<br /> <br /> Avengers/Legends seems mostly unchanged.<br /> <br /> Ammm so slashers actively create Tainted places around them, yikes. While I get that they generally don't use Bygones, something in the style of Saika from Durarara!! (or any cursed, sentient weapon of murder) could serves as a nice plot hook.<br /> <br /> Brutes and masks are also the same, but I don't remember if in 1e they were also bound by compulsions and bans. I think it was more of Legends territory.<br /> <br /> So psychos were renamed Hypnos. They also seem to be more social, saying the truth, and less &quot;on the edge&quot;.<br /> <br /> Freaks were renamed Undesirables, for obvious reasons. They are also less about physical deformity than social pariah. Mutants is when that rejection manifests itself in flesh.<br /> <br /> Geniuses and maniacs were renamed Virtuosos and Puppeteers. Still all about manipulating people through mind games and strategies in order to murder.<br /> <br /> So each undertaking has its own Tell, and Avengers are forced to let people know that they were the ones responsible- to &quot;warn others&quot; that they are coming to punish them.<br /> <br /> Talents and frailties are still a thing.<br /> <br /> The Legend quote is TERRIFYING.<br /> <br /> Yeah, Legends are stories made flesh, and the internet allowing them to spread worldwide is absolutely terrifying.<br /> <br /> The Painted Bride sounds really familiar for some reason- I am pretty sure she was mentioned before.<br /> <br /> So scourges have example Dread Powers. Nice.<br /> <br /> The Brute's quote is somewhat ironic.<br /> <br /> Masks are disgusting.<br /> <br /> Charmers unifying slashers together into cabals is really bad for hunters.<br /> <br /> Ah, so hypnos are idealists- well, at least they have goals in life.<br /> <br /> So yeah, hypnos are quit different from 1e Psychos, IMO, and they LOVE to monologue.<br /> <br /> You can almost feel sorry for the undesirables.. at least, until they try to kill you.<br /> <br /> So yeah, it seems that cabals have higher tendency to form due to the slasher epidemic.. or maybe that the slasher epidemic is the result of cabals fueling it. Chicken and an egg, so to speak.<br /> <br /> Mutants are disgusting.<br /> <br /> The Virtuoso's quote is plain awesome.<br /> <br /> Puppeteers are yet the other monologuing villains.<br /> <br /> It is nice that every Undertaking could be seen as the greatest threat on humanity on its own.<br /> <br /> Y echoes in the back of my mind for some slasher reference, but I can't recall from where.<br /> <br /> War between slashers is terrible- it seems that the Driver is not the only slasher devoted into discovering the secrets of the God Machine.<br /> <br /> So the Tell is the negative of the Code- the Code reminds hunters why they kill monsters, the Tell reminds them why they kill people, and both serve to remind them that they &quot;are not monsters&quot;. I guess that both are wrong, to some degree :P<br /> <br /> Si someone can turn ripper before they kill, but can be stopped during that &quot;transition&quot; from falling into full slasherhood.<br /> <br /> I think that there are not exact details about how exactly an hunter becomes a ripper- and how you could restore them? Like, regaining Integrity is stated, but again, the exact details are murky.<br /> <br /> So slashers may have Potency. Yikes.<br /> <br /> So once an hunter (or anyone) turns slasher, they Integrity falls to 0- and if they manage to gain back Integrity before they murder they can be redeemed. Again, I would have preferred if it was outright stated instead of having to reverse engineer it.<br /> <br /> Ah, here are the rules- sorry for judging you too soon!<br /> <br /> Wait.. did I missed the favored attribute per Undertaking? I don't think I see it...<br /> <br /> Also- FIVE RATING ATTRIBUTE FOR FREE?? Yikes.<br /> <br /> So scourges may have integrity, but they are forever marked by blood? Like, they can regain their sanity, but they are still motivated towards murder and death.<br /> <br /> Ah- finally, how one can fall into slasherhood.<br /> <br /> Cool.<br /> <br /> But why would a conspiracy allow a suspect slasher to leave in one piece?<br /> <br /> Slasher Merits- Yikes.<br /> <br /> So now monsters fear slashers? YIKES.<br /> <br /> Cheiron are disgusting.<br /> <br /> The Council is indeed perfect for Slasher Chronicles.<br /> <br /> Wait- we get Endowments before VASCU and Nine Stars? Or maybe the editor forgot to add them to the chapter?<br /> <br /> So here are the actual setting writeups.<br /> <br /> Yeah- Philadelphia's cabal is scary.<br /> <br /> The Sower really shows how a Legend becomes something unearthly, a true monster beyond human definition.<br /> <br /> THE HUNT CLUB IS HERE<br /> <br /> Yeah, with Jack the Ripper, London is a must.<br /> <br /> I must say that Smiling Jack sounds more like a Psycho than a puppeteer, but he could work as both.<br /> <br /> Weaponized ghosts? Oh the Council is in trouble.<br /> <br /> I start to wonder what would it take for the Ashwood to clash against the Hunt Club yet rise stronger from it, instead of shattered by it.<br /> <br /> Yeah, the Council is indeed here.<br /> <br /> Yeah, New Delhi is scary.<br /> <br /> Yeah, Network Zero is a must- also, a new compact! Sounds like an Hindu version of the Union, but still cool.<br /> <br /> And of course we are getting Hong Kong.<br /> <br /> I SAID THAT THE EATER OF NAMES IS THE BASTARD! I SAID IT I SAID IT HAHAHAHAHAHAHAHA<br /> <br /> Oh, that's all?... I WANT MORE SETTINGS!<br /> <br /> And that's it! I have finished reading Hunter 2e! I'll make another post about updating the Mysteres's Endowment, probably today or tomorrow. Feel free to share your closing thoughts about the book, and hope you enjoyed reading my thoughts about it!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-04T13:55:41-08:00","id":1372810,"title":"","content":"So time for<b> Rites du Cheval</b> update-<br /> <br /> <b>Concept:</b> Les Mysteres teaches their members how to allow the spirits ride their flesh while maintaining control, appeasing the gods and gaining their blessings through rituals and discipline.<br /> <br /> So, the Rites have two main feature- they are ritualistic, and they work by allowing the spirits to ride one's flesh. In 1e, they also have some tie to the Status of the conspiracy, which is meant to represent how fractured their structure is. With them breaking apart and then forced to rebuild, it makes sense to keep the Status requirement in some form, but the main question is how. Some way to regulate the use of the Rites through the hunter's self control also seems appropriate. As such, we have four main features to consider- ritualism, possession, Status and self control.<br /> <br /> The ritualistic character of the Rites makes me think that perhaps a structure similar to that of Benedictions is the most appropriate one. My personal instinct is that in order to tie Status into the Endowment, we could perhaps use Status as the dice pool the hunter must roll when activating their Endowments. That brings the question for &quot;why would the popularity of the hunter in the conspiracy influence their ability to control the spirits&quot; kind of question. The answer would be that spirits recognize and respect hierarchies- and by recognizing the hunters of the Mysteres as emissaries, they grant it power. Status in the Mysteres would be treated as an<b> Honorary Rank</b> among spirits, and as such the more respected is the hunter in the conspiracy, the more the spirits will be willing to work with the hunter instead of trying to possess them. That may also be one of the reasons that the conspiracy has broken down- as the conspiracy spread too thin, the meaning of the Status - and as such, the Rank is bestowed with it - lost its meaning, and the spirits moved in to take opportunity of the now defenseless hunters. Making the spirits to respect the Emissaries again was probably one of the first steps in rebuilding the conspiracy.<br /> <br /> Now that we have the basis of the system, let's decide how it works- as a ritualistic Endowment, the basic roll would be <b>Resolve + Expression + Status (Les Mysteres)</b>. Losing all Status in the conspiracy would make the hunter unable to use their Endowments, and any such attempt would simply turn them into the spirits plaything. The Endowments also require some appeasement, which would take the form of the cost. As for modifiers, I tends think that using appeasements with higher cost than necessary (that is, requiring Resources to gain them) should give a +1 modifier for each excess point of Resources. All in all, I think that this is how I would structure the Rites du Cheval's basic roll-<br /> <br /> <b>Cost:</b> Appeasement (see each ritual for specifics)<br /> <br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> Resolve + Expression + Status (Les Mysteres)<br /> <br /> <b>Action:</b> Extended (15 minutes, blah blah details about how Successes needs to be accumulated blah blah)<br /> <br /> <b>Duration:</b> One hour per Status<br /> <br /> <b>Roll Results:</b><br /> <br /> <b>Success:</b> the ritual draws the spirits and activates as required. You gain the Ridden Condition at the end of the ritual.<br /> <br /> <b>Exceptional Success:</b> your actions made the spirits dance to your song and the Shadow celebrate with joy. Either reduce the number of needed Successes by your Status or gain the Inspired Condition in the end of the ritual.<br /> <br /> <b>Failure:</b> the spirits don't listen to your prayers. You either abandon the ritual or continue and suffer from the Stumbled Condition<br /> <br /> <b>Dramatic Failure:</b> your appeasements and rituals have failed you, and the spirits lurk into your mind. The ritual fails, and you suffer from the Possessed Condition.<br /> <br /> <b>Condition: Ridden</b><br /> The spirits share the burden of the mortal coil with the hunter, taking allowing them to ignore the pain and fear of battle. The hunter can ignore wound penalties, and any attempt to force upon them any fear related Condition (such as Shaken, Frightened or Spooked) suffers from a -2 modifier. <br /> <b>Possible Sources:</b> Success in the Rites du Cheval ritual<br /> <b>Beat:</b> N/A<br /> <b>Resolution:</b> the Condition is resolved at the end of the ritual's duration without granting a Beat.<br /> <br /> <b>Condition: Possessed</b><br /> The spirits of the otherworld have crept into your mind, and their cacophony of alien voices cloud your judgement until you fulfill their will. The hunter suffers -2 modifier for all Perception rolls for any action which does not satisfy the spirit's desires.<br /> <b>Possible Sources:</b> Dramatic Failure in a Rites du Cheval roll.<br /> <b>Beat:</b> every time the desires of the spirit hinder you or your cell's efforts, gain a Beat<br /> <b>Resolution:</b> when the spirit crawls into your mind, it comes with specific demands. Once the spirit gains what it desired, you can shed this Condition and gain a Beat. Exorcism may also resolve this Condition, yet then no Beat is gained, and the hunter would suffer a -1 modifier for their next attempt to activate the Rites du Cheval.<br /> <br /> So now that we have those basic mechanics, let's try to break it apart into numbers.<br /> <br /> Appeasements are consumable ingredients, which gives a -2 to the Endowment. As the Rites should be quicker and more active than Benedictions, I have decided it should take minutes to activate them instead of hours, and as such we have another -4. Each action beyond the first one (as gaining Successes is the goal) it would give -1 for every Success above 5. The Dramatic Failure enforce a backlash equivalent of -2, but as it is only the Dramatic Failure I would treat it as -1. The Ridden Condition balances it with +1, and I think that the passive benefit of an Honorary Rank is the equivalent of a +4. The Rites also last for a number of hours, which is a +2. I am not counting the effect of the Inspired Condition, as it is only when you gain an Exceptional Success, so +0. Let's sum it up-<br /> <br /> -2 - 4 - 1 +1 + 4 + 2 + 0 = 0.<br /> <br /> Ah, so the dice roll itself is outright balanced. Nice. That also mean that every ritual is going to be required to be balanced by its own, mostly by the number of Successes needed. We could say that every hunter knows immediately the <b>Calling Down the Thunder</b> Endowment, which is the basic dice pool which serves only to gain the Ridden Condition. That Rite is the most basic ritual, requiring any minor sacrifice for the spirits in exchange for gaining the basic benefit, and which serves as a gate for the rest of the Endowments of the conspiracy.<br /> <br /> Now, let's update two sample Endowments and see what we gain from it.<br /> <br /> <b>Skin of the Loa</b><br /> The hunter learn to wear the spirits on their own flesh, allowing their ephemera to shield the hunter from danger. The spirit, in return, demands the blood of those the hunter's enemies.<br /> <b>Successes: 5</b><br /> <b>Appeasement:</b> a sheet of paper drenched in wine <br /> <b>Effect:</b> the hunter's Armor increase by 2. However, while the Endowment is active, the hunter gains the Obsession Condition towards their enemies as long as the Endowment is active.<br /> <br /> So, as the Endowment was meant to be simple and basic in 1e, I didn't wanted to increase the number of Success above 5. Also, the table for Endowment effects does not seem to detail the modifier for extra Armor, so I have just took the value as a modifier. The Condition balances it as a backlash with -2.<br /> <br /> <b>Hands of Raphael</b><br /> Channeling spirits of healing and medicine, the hunter is gifted with the legendary lay of hands in order to supports their cellmates in the pursuit of the Vigil.<br /> <b>Successes: 7</b><br /> <b>Appeasement:</b> Grounded silver powder.<br /> <b>Effect:</b> for each Success the hunter gains in the Endowment, the hunter gains an &quot;healing token&quot;. The hunter can expand one such token in order to heal a level of bashing damage, two for lethal and four for aggravated. The hunter can also remove the Sick or Poisoned Tilts in exchange for two such tokens. However, while carrying the mantle of the healer, the hunter pays a price with their own body, gaining the Sick Tilt while the Endowment is active.<br /> <br /> Now, it is very hard to estimate the amount of healing gained from the Endowment. As such, we can at least heal 7 health levels, so we start at 7. Grounded silver requires at least resources of 3 I estimate, which would enforce extra -2 cost. That leaves us at 5. The increased target number brings another -2, bringing us to +3. The Sick tilt balances it to 0.<br /> <br /> So yeah, as you can see, while the Endowment design rules do help to balance out the Endowments, yet when you try to get somewhat creative with it quantifying the actual effects and costs becomes a bit difficult. At least they allow you make the Endowments somewhat balanced, and it would take some time to get adjusted to the rules. Still, I think they work, even if perhaps the Rites du Cheval, not to mention the Hands of Raphael, were not the wisest choice for a first time conversion experiment :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-04T14:10:48-08:00","id":1372818,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1365834-lostlight-reads-hunter-2e?p=1372692#post1372692\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I SAID THAT THE EATER OF NAMES IS THE BASTARD! I SAID IT I SAID IT HAHAHAHAHAHAHAHA</div> </div> </div> </div>Heheheheheh.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-04T14:24:33-08:00","id":1372821,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1365834-lostlight-reads-hunter-2e?p=1372583#post1372583\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ahh, the Keepers of the Source are very underappreciated compact. Is it ok if I ask some questions about how you see their perspective about the sites they protect, and some specifics regarding the sub factions?</div> </div> </div> </div>I see their philosophies more or less as they have been in 1e- other than the Dynasts. The Dynasts would have some greater emphasis on not only moderating between the two sides, but also to make sure that the compact would survive, grow, and leave legacy after it. Heck, maybe some even dream about it growing into a conspiracy. The Dynasts want the compact to have a lasting existence, instead of &quot;just&quot; a temporary protest movement. They want to save Mother Earth, and for that they must have a better understanding of ley lines and how to work with them, as well as an infrastructure for their work.<br /> <br /> As for the sites themselves, they would probably be a form of a mysterious place- even though none of the presented forms fit what they probably seek to protect. Sources would be a new form of a mysterious place, one which could power the Endowments of hunters.. or the Dread Powers of monsters. Tainted places would probably be seen as Sources which were corrupted by monsters, while sentient places are where Mother Earth's rage incarnates into form- and those places must be pacified, either through ritual or, in the case of Redgrove's followers, the death of those who abuse Her. My personal view is that the Keepers have some truth in their claims- places like Loci and Hallows serve as sacred shrines of Mother Earth's magic, and by harvesting that magic the monsters inhibit the natural flow, just like how humans shape their surroundings and use the natural resources for technological purposes. Coal by its own serves no special purpose in nature, but burning it harms the ecosystem. There is &quot;magical pollution&quot; in the world, and draining Sources from magic does influence the natural flow, but murdering witches for harnessing Sources would be like murdering a driver for burning oil in their car. So there is some justice for their claims, but things need to be taken into proportion :P<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, while I think your Les mysteres write-up is a good way to show them as a &quot;re-building&quot; conspiracy, I admittedly prefer them back as as more disparate with the unique factions. </div> </div> </div>I only work with what I have- I could have just used their 1e state as is, but I prefer my work to be consistent with 2e. Also, those many cults and factions are still around in this writeup- I have simply decided to focus around that faction which still calls itself Les Mysteres, and how they work to rebuild from the ruins. Other factions around the world may have similar goals and different methods, or perhaps instead prefer to develop their own local brand of shamanism over the syncretic faith of the Mysteres.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-04T14:33:34-08:00","id":1372827,"title":"","content":"Oh, I am also going to add some closing thoughts about Hunter 2e in general, probably tomorrow after the end of the Kickstarter. I need some time to digest everything, after all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-04T15:29:58-08:00","id":1372837,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1365834-lostlight-reads-hunter-2e?p=1372821#post1372821\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I see their philosophies more or less as they have been in 1e- other than the Dynasts. The Dynasts would have some greater emphasis on not only moderating between the two sides, but also to make sure that the compact would survive, grow, and leave legacy after it. Heck, maybe some even dream about it growing into a conspiracy. The Dynasts want the compact to have a lasting existence, instead of &amp;quot;just&amp;quot; a temporary protest movement. They want to save Mother Earth, and for that they must have a better understanding of ley lines and how to work with them, as well as an infrastructure for their work.<br /> <br /> As for the sites themselves, they would probably be a form of a mysterious place- even though none of the presented forms fit what they probably seek to protect. Sources would be a new form of a mysterious place, one which could power the Endowments of hunters.. or the Dread Powers of monsters. Tainted places would probably be seen as Sources which were corrupted by monsters, while sentient places are where Mother Earth's rage incarnates into form- and those places must be pacified, either through ritual or, in the case of Redgrove's followers, the death of those who abuse Her. My personal view is that the Keepers have some truth in their claims- places like Loci and Hallows serve as sacred shrines of Mother Earth's magic, and by harvesting that magic the monsters inhibit the natural flow, just like how humans shape their surroundings and use the natural resources for technological purposes. Coal by its own serves no special purpose in nature, but burning it harms the ecosystem. There is &amp;quot;magical pollution&amp;quot; in the world, and draining Sources from magic does influence the natural flow, but murdering witches for harnessing Sources would be like murdering a driver for burning oil in their car. So there is some justice for their claims, but things need to be taken into proportion :P<br /> <br /> <br /> I only work with what I have- I could have just used their 1e state as is, but I prefer my work to be consistent with 2e. Also, those many cults and factions are still around in this writeup- I have simply decided to focus around that faction which still calls itself Les Mysteres, and how they work to rebuild from the ruins. Other factions around the world may have similar goals and different methods, or perhaps instead prefer to develop their own local brand of shamanism over the syncretic faith of the Mysteres.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wow, you answered all my questions about the compact overall and the one specifically for the Dynasts, impressive. Just 3 questions is all I have<br /> <br /> 1. Considering how extreme the Hand of the Mother is, do you give them any redeeming qualities (or simply some more in depth stuff) so they arent simply knight templars (sorry if you dont get what I mean, that's from tv tropes)<br /> <br /> 2. I see the Children of Gaia are still extreme pacifists. Much like my previous question, I kinda struggle to see how you can play as a member of that Philosophy, as the monsters often fought dont give a shit about pacifists asking them to stop. So basically, what do they accomplish that gives their efforts credibility instead of slaughtered or completely ignored?<br /> <br /> 3. Originally a Dynasts question, but you answered perfectly (I can even see what would be potential flaws of the group). My new question concerns Tainted places. Do you think Keepers would have the same approach to them as your compact, the Domus, or have a different method to purifying it (likely concerning monsters to be killed/negotiated with)<br /> <br /> Concerning the Les Mysteres, by the way, I am so sorry. I did not mean that as a criticism. I do see it as a very clean transition to a re-building phase and did notice that the different beliefs were there, just less emphasized. I guess what I meant to say was, much like the Cainites, i love how a big focus of them was how disparate they were.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-05T04:55:29-08:00","id":1372938,"title":"","content":"So as we reach the end of the Kickstarter, here are my closing thoughts about Hunter 2e-<br /> <br /> - Overall, I really enjoyed the book. It manages to keep the feeling of how the Vigil is powered by desperate hope, mortals taking a stance against the darkness, the place of hunters as underdogs and the fear of the unknown.<br /> <br /> - I really did enjoyed the history section, even though some of the parts about how former splats were fallen/absorbed by others is controversial. The dynamism of the setting is an interesting choice, and I get that the team wanted to give hunter some more modern history by having former groups change and fall. The main issue is Merrick, for the level of how it would make sense depends strongly about whether the writeup refers to the conspiracy who made the dreamwalking children or the children themselves.<br /> <br /> - I generally enjoyed the writeups for all compacts and conspiracies, and I did liked how some tweaks and plot hooks were added to them. I am perfectly fine with VASCU going private, for example. Still, the constant feeling of dynamism in the splat writeups is a bit strange and unconventional, and I didn't expected them to be so similar to how things were in 1e, format wise. I must admit that SWORN is pretty bland IMO, and while their whole angle about cryptids and the difference between &quot;monsters which are part of the ecosystem&quot; vs &quot;invasive species&quot; is really cool, a lot of their writeup makes them feel &quot;like a Union for Native Americans&quot;. I, of course, have no issue with having a Native American group, but I would have preferred it to have a greater emphasis on what makes them different (that is, cryptids, ecosystem and anti colonialism) than how they are &quot;just&quot; a compact focused around protecting Native Americans. The Council of Bones is also no in my top favorite groups, but the Storytelling Chapter and the Slasher Chronicles did worked to give them more character, admitting their arrogance and flaws instead of &quot;a just and virtuous conspiracy&quot;. Their lack of history also makes me hard to enjoy them, writeup wise. Again, they have a lot of cool things about them, but the reasons detailed in this thread they are just not &quot;click&quot; for me as other organizations- but I like them more after the ST chapter than when I first read their writeup. Nine Stars were really cool, and I really enjoyed reading them. I must say that I am surprised to see how much attention did the AKD got through the book (including the example settings), which makes me wonder about why they are not in the core, considering that the core speaks about them so much (yeah, they have a very basic writeup in the ST chapter, but you get what I mean). Also, please give me the writeups for the Five Roses Empire and the Los Angelitos!<br /> <br /> - As for the core rules, I am a big fan of giving hunters Touchstones. The Code being dependent on how the hunter understands the situation really helps with the issues about &quot;people vs monsters&quot;, even though sometimes the writeup almost feels apologetic for the fans for the decision- yes, there was a controversy about it, and I appreciate that the book recognize it, but I think that such explanations should be presented in the community instead of in the book itself, but it is still for the team to acknowledge the issue. I did enjoyed the description of the Code and how it takes form, an oath the hunter takes upon themselves after being pushed to the edge. Tactics were also really great, and felt very organic in their presentation. While Tactics, Touchstones, the Code and Risking Willpower are all great, I kind of wish that the book would have presented some other &quot;unique&quot; features of being an hunter, be it thinks like Skill Tricks from Mirrors or things like that. Having the Supernatural Tolerance merit from Hurt Locker and allowing Third Tier Hunters to buy it could have also been a nice touch. You know, some extra things which would make hunters feel &quot;special&quot;, even though I understand that the team wanted to focus around how the greatest source of power that hunters have is their teamwork. Costume gear could have been a part of the rules instead of an appendix, IMO.<br /> <br /> - Now, while I did enjoyed the Dread Powers and the roster of monsters which was presented, there are a few things which kind of bother me. Among the Dread Powers, I really wish that Infernal would not have been tied to fire manipulation as it is, for that Dread Power also marks a monster as been a target for Castigation. I would have been satisfied with it simply granting a True Name and some basic demonic quality for those who hold it- after all, Hell has ice as well as fire. The other thing is about the monsters themselves- I am a big fan of how hunter Incorporated monsters from urban legends to the setting, but sometimes it felt like those monsters are too &quot;just like in legend&quot;, and I wanted to seem some sort of twist which ties them to the greater CofD setting- simply mentioning how &quot;brain eating ants&quot; look like &quot;they are made of brass&quot;, for example, could have been an awesome easter egg, IMO, and would have added a twist beyond the regular legend. Now, another complaint is that while the book and the lexicon talks about all the varieties of monsters, there isn't a specialized section for each &quot;archetype&quot; or &quot;breed&quot; of monsters like there was in 1e. Vampires, skinwalkers, witches, reanimated, fairies, revenants, mummies, demons, mythics, mutants and/or cryptids being described in the monster section, as well as suggesting which Dread Powers are appropriate for them, could have been really cool IMO. I understand that the book wanted to move from &quot;hunters hunt the protagonists of other gamelines&quot;, but those archetypes could cover a wide range of monstrosities beyond the exact protagonists- and besides, as those protagonists are the most organized and populous monsters, the chances are the hunters do hunt them. Again, I love how Hunter tied itself to urban legends, but I would have liked at least some discussion about how the book suggest building those monsters in Hunter. Beyond that, what that I felt was missing the most was WHY there are more monsters than the usual. Either what hunters think about it, or what the monsters think about it. That section was very &quot;from the Hunter's POV&quot;, and I felt that some discussion about the monsters' perspective was missing, and I would have liked to see it.<br /> <br /> - Let's put it this way- Mysterious Places are just awesome. They are a really good addition to Hunter, and they add a lot of character to the setting. I only wish that there was some more extensive details about local compacts and conspiracies around the presented Mysterious Places, as well as the local monsters in them, in order to turn them into full settings. I did felt like how none antagonistic mysterious places were missing, like Loci and Hallows, which could have made things somewhat more complicated for hunters. Bygones are also really cool, and the fact that every hunter may access them is a great addition for Hunter (as some people pointed out that having all relics limited to the AKD didn't really made sense)- but I do wish that the AKD would have got a more detailed writeup in order to give a deeper research for how their Endowments differ from the Bygones of other groups. Also, I would reaaaaaaaally want an example Bygone list.<br /> <br /> - Now, the Slasher Chronicles chapter is something I am a bit ambivalent about. It has a lot of good things, I do like how Undertaking were presented, and the example settings are outright awesome. On the other hand, just like I didn't really felt the &quot;monsters' side of the story&quot; in the previous chapter, I also don't really feel the slasher's one. The example settings help with it, but it is still not enough, IMO. I mean, when I read the original Slasher sourcebook, I had nightmares for a week, mostly because it went deep into the psych of the slashers. In here, their presentation sometimes makes them feel like puppets, more like blank pages and without much of personality other than they murder. Again, the example settings help with it, but compared to the strix and the idigam and the reapers and alchemists and so forth, the horror of the slashers feel more superficial. Again, probably because the book focus mostly on the Hunter side and not on the Slasher side. I also didn't really liked how the rise in slashers means that monsters become less active- as it outright contradicts the rest of the book, turning it into more of a shard instead of an optional addition to the setting. It seems like just how the book divides hunter into 3 different playstyles by Tier, it also makes the Slasher Chronicles into an alternative universe instead of the canon one, which I would prefer it to be otherwise. While this section does indeed refer to the possible origins of the &quot;slasher epidemic&quot;, none of them really caught my attention, saying the truth. I would have liked if the example settings were to leave some plot hooks about whatever is the source which makes slashers, but unfortunately it is not really the case (other than Hong Kong- Chris Allen, you are a mad genius). I also kind of wonder how to use the &quot;slasher epidemic&quot; in places where there isn't much of a &quot;slasher culture&quot; nor a lot of historic serial killers (like where I live, thankfully, and let's hope it stays this way). Also, the lack of cabals as a thing was really disappointing. It could have added an whole new layer to the slasher chronicles, serving as a dark mirror for compacts and present some of the &quot;slasher's side in the story&quot;.<br /> <br /> - now, the Storyteller's chapter was indeed really cool, and gave a LOT of character to the game. I only wish that cults would have got a bigger writeup, but I get why they are in this chapter and not in the antagonists one. I still needs to adjust to the new Endowment creation rules, but they do serve, at the very least, as pretty good guidelines. Overall, it was a really good chapter to read.<br /> <br /> So to sum it up- while it may look like I complain about Hunter, it is far from the case- sure, there is a lot of focus about what I didn't liked in this post, but it is because saying &quot;everything here is AWESOME&quot; could be too boring. I enjoyed a lot of what the book had to offer, and it was full of cool plot hooks and ideas for the game. The biggest things which bothered me could be summed up as the lack of having the &quot;monsters' side of the story&quot;, the dissonance between the &quot;core&quot; setting and the &quot;slashers chronicles&quot; setting, the lack of focus around &quot;monstrous archetypes&quot;, the lack of a section about cabals, and the lack of example Bygones. Some more personal complaints would be the general &quot;lack of twists&quot; in the presentation of the example monsters and that the Mysterious Places were not as developed as the example settings in the Slasher Chronicles. Everything else is very minor, and entirely depends on your personal taste.<br /> <br /> And that's it! Hope you had fun reading my thought on the Kickstarter, and let's wait to see what Tending the Flames has in store for us! (And maybe we can still get the last stretch goal. Maybe).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":503,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","user":"LostLight","date":". 03-05-2020, 07:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-05T08:35:53-08:00","id":1372978,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1365834-lostlight-reads-hunter-2e?p=1370994#post1370994\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I still feel that the Union are, like the worst nightmare that monsters have. The last thing you want as a monster is to discover that the whole neighborhood is against you, and that they will come at you with everything they have.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Union is the embodiment of how when things get really bad, humans tend to cooperate and have each other's backs. Damn straight that's a monster's worst nightmare.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25922-alchemical","name":"Alchemical","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-05T11:06:42-08:00","id":1373008,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alchemical</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1365834-lostlight-reads-hunter-2e?p=1372978#post1372978\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Union is the embodiment of how when things get really bad, humans tend to cooperate and have each other's backs. Damn straight that's a monster's worst nightmare.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would say all the organizations can be a monsters worst nightmare<br /> <br /> The ashwood abbey is what happens when the elite realize they are the elite, and decide that monsters arent scary, but incredibly fun creatures to play &quot;games&quot; with. Not to mention getting cozy with other monsters that you thought were YOUR allies.<br /> <br /> The Long Night is when humanity decides monsters must be fought and that hope is never lost as long as they CAN fight and worse, inspire others to join the Vigil and bring hope<br /> <br /> Network Zero is when...well, it's easy to see how that players out<br /> <br /> Really, I can see every groups being a worst nightmare to monsters. I think it's actually a good way to see what makes a monster scared of them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-05T13:46:48-08:00","id":1373063,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1365834-lostlight-reads-hunter-2e?p=1372938#post1372938\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So as we reach the end of the Kickstarter, here are my closing thoughts about Hunter 2e- &lt; Awesome sum-up &gt;</div> </div> </div> </div> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1870-mlvalentine\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1870_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1870\" data-vbnamecard=\"1870\">mlvalentine</a> , if I may, I really agree with everything <b>LostLight</b> has written. I would only add a minor nitpick - <i>Mythic</i>, as term is mentioned in Lexicon, but not showing in the previews text, really. If I may advised how to use it more, it could come up in SWORN write-up as '<i>Mythics</i> are creatures of our forefathers', or something like that. Also, mentioning in main write-up of SWORN that in present it's global compact, connecting various ethnical groups around the world, beside it's only Native Americans roots, made it feel much more 'global' and 'corebook worth', marking it much more open to interpretations by STs. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-06T11:06:47-08:00","id":1373230,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1365834-lostlight-reads-hunter-2e?p=1372837#post1372837\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wow, you answered all my questions about the compact overall and the one specifically for the Dynasts, impressive. Just 3 questions is all I have<br /> <br /> 1. Considering how extreme the Hand of the Mother is, do you give them any redeeming qualities (or simply some more in depth stuff) so they arent simply knight templars (sorry if you dont get what I mean, that's from tv tropes)</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I think that the most redeeming quality of the Hand is that they are, in essence, hunters- the Children of Gaia may be &quot;nicer&quot;, but the Vigil is not about being nice. It is about taking a stand against the darkness and fighting the enemy. The Hand knows that monsters abuse Mother Earth, and as such it is up to them to stop the abuse. Monsters are monsters, and their actions taint the world- and someone must put an end for their selfish actions. The Hand, as extremist as it may be, follow the Code much better than the Children, and as such are less likely to just &quot;snap&quot; one day and fall into slasherhood.. as long as they care enough on &quot;collateral damage&quot;, f course.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2. I see the Children of Gaia are still extreme pacifists. Much like my previous question, I kinda struggle to see how you can play as a member of that Philosophy, as the monsters often fought dont give a shit about pacifists asking them to stop. So basically, what do they accomplish that gives their efforts credibility instead of slaughtered or completely ignored? </div> </div> </div>What they try to do is to teach monsters how to treat the sacred places with respect. They believe that if they could make monsters take their claims seriously, Mother Earth would be saved and no blood would be spilled. By studying the ley lines and understanding the flow, they can not only discover other Sources, but also show the monsters that they know what they are talking about, and hopefully start converting/redeeming them. Can they do it? Does that philosophy stable? Who knows? There is a string chance that the Children would eventually collapse after understanding how futile their efforts are. There is a chance that the compact would collapse for the same reason. If so, I could totally see the Children just &quot;breaking&quot; and turning into a Cabal, especially if there are enough Lucids among them (see Night Horrors: the Unbidden if you don't know what a Lucid is)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 3. Originally a Dynasts question, but you answered perfectly (I can even see what would be potential flaws of the group). My new question concerns Tainted places. Do you think Keepers would have the same approach to them as your compact, the Domus, or have a different method to purifying it (likely concerning monsters to be killed/negotiated with) </div> </div> </div>The Domus as written mostly seek to &quot;cleanse&quot; those sites- which means remove the supernatural force from the root. The Keepers, on the other hand, are likely to try and &quot;correct&quot; the Tainted, probably by using a combination of resonance and lay line manipulation in order to maintain the supernatural nature of the site, yet remove the dark effects (that is, Dread Powers and Potency, basically &quot;killing&quot; the monster but replacing it with a Source). Sentient places are another issue- as those sites are seen as a manifestation of Mother Earth's rage, and by quelling the rage they should simply cease to exist.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Concerning the Les Mysteres, by the way, I am so sorry. I did not mean that as a criticism. I do see it as a very clean transition to a re-building phase and did notice that the different beliefs were there, just less emphasized. I guess what I meant to say was, much like the Cainites, i love how a big focus of them was how disparate they were. </div> </div> </div>No issue- I got what your intentions were. I have just wanted to clarify my choice for the Mysteres's update, and why I chose to present them in their rebuilding state instead of the original writeup.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":503,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","user":"LostLight","date":". 03-06-2020, 04:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-06T17:21:03-08:00","id":1373282,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1365834-lostlight-reads-hunter-2e?p=1373230#post1373230\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, I think that the most redeeming quality of the Hand is that they are, in essence, hunters- the Children of Gaia may be &quot;nicer&quot;, but the Vigil is not about being nice. It is about taking a stand against the darkness and fighting the enemy. The Hand knows that monsters abuse Mother Earth, and as such it is up to them to stop the abuse. Monsters are monsters, and their actions taint the world- and someone must put an end for their selfish actions. The Hand, as extremist as it may be, follow the Code much better than the Children, and as such are less likely to just &quot;snap&quot; one day and fall into slasherhood.. as long as they care enough on &quot;collateral damage&quot;, f course.<br /> <br /> <br /> What they try to do is to teach monsters how to treat the sacred places with respect. They believe that if they could make monsters take their claims seriously, Mother Earth would be saved and no blood would be spilled. By studying the ley lines and understanding the flow, they can not only discover other Sources, but also show the monsters that they know what they are talking about, and hopefully start converting/redeeming them. Can they do it? Does that philosophy stable? Who knows? There is a string chance that the Children would eventually collapse after understanding how futile their efforts are. There is a chance that the compact would collapse for the same reason. If so, I could totally see the Children just &quot;breaking&quot; and turning into a Cabal, especially if there are enough Lucids among them (see Night Horrors: the Unbidden if you don't know what a Lucid is)<br /> <br /> <br /> The Domus as written mostly seek to &quot;cleanse&quot; those sites- which means remove the supernatural force from the root. The Keepers, on the other hand, are likely to try and &quot;correct&quot; the Tainted, probably by using a combination of resonance and lay line manipulation in order to maintain the supernatural nature of the site, yet remove the dark effects (that is, Dread Powers and Potency, basically &quot;killing&quot; the monster but replacing it with a Source). Sentient places are another issue- as those sites are seen as a manifestation of Mother Earth's rage, and by quelling the rage they should simply cease to exist.<br /> <br /> <br /> No issue- I got what your intentions were. I have just wanted to clarify my choice for the Mysteres's update, and why I chose to present them in their rebuilding state instead of the original writeup.</div> </div> </div> </div>1. Ok, I like this. The Hand as the faction that's willing to take immediate action, to risk their lives for Mother Earth no questions asked, while also staying to the Code because of the extremism, not in spite of it.<br /> <br /> 2. Ahh, so the Children are probably have the most occult know how with Ley Lines. I suppose another advantage is they look to less direct (and less violent) methods to save Source Pools. I actually do find that interesting though, for mortals to FINALLY have something they know about to a greater degree than a gameline splat . EDIT: and yeah I do know the Lucid. The plot hook of the Children becoming little more than that after &quot;snapping&quot; is an interesting angle<br /> <br /> 3. That sounds like a very fun way to deal with Tainted places actually. Would be cool to see how a tainted place changes when Keepers purify it into a Source pool<br /> <br /> 4. ahh ok. If you do continue making write ups for orgs. that are absorbed/defunct now, I would like to see how you see them &quot;re-building&quot;. <br /> <br /> Ok, I'm really sorry since the questions must be getting annoying, but I do have just one more, I promise. What about Source pools in urban areas? Certainly, not ALL of them are in places of nature.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24173,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","user":"Primordial newcomer","date":". 03-06-2020, 08:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-07T15:35:13-08:00","id":1373447,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1365834-lostlight-reads-hunter-2e?p=1373282#post1373282\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 4. ahh ok. If you do continue making write ups for orgs. that are absorbed/defunct now, I would like to see how you see them &quot;re-building&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>That would be a subject for its own thread, won't it? :P<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Ok, I'm really sorry since the questions must be getting annoying, but I do have just one more, I promise. What about Source pools in urban areas? Certainly, not ALL of them are in places of nature. </div> </div> </div>Like you said, they can manifest in urban places- and the Keepers would protect them just the same, even though I assume that urban architecture could influence them, and as such the Keepers would object shaping the surroundings. Feng shui and all of that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-07T16:03:55-08:00","id":1373451,"title":"","content":"